  const TX={"neuromodulators":{"n": "Neuromodulators", "c": "injectables", "s": "Injections that relax the muscles behind frown lines, forehead lines and crow's feet, and for neck bands and jawline contouring.", "i": "Neuromodulators are prescription Wrinkle-Relaxing Injections that temporarily relax the muscles that form expression lines. At Mediworks in South Surrey, treatment is performed by our Naturopathic Doctors after a Naturopathic Aesthetic Consultation and facial assessment.", "f": ["About 15–30 min", "Typically every 3–4 months", "Usually none", "Usually 1–2 weeks"], "g": ["Frown lines between the brows", "Forehead lines and crow's feet", "Neck bands (platysmal bands)", "Jawline contouring (Nefertiti lift)"], "h": [["Assess", "Your clinician reviews how your face moves at rest and with expression, and maps the treatment points.", "10 min"], ["Prepare", "The skin is cleansed. Numbing is usually not needed.", "5 min"], ["Treat", "A small number of injections with a very fine needle.", "10 min"]], "x": [["Same day", "Small raised marks usually settle within an hour. Stay upright for 4 hours and avoid rubbing the area."], ["Days 3–5", "Muscle movement usually begins to soften."], ["Week 2", "The effect is usually fully visible. A follow-up check is booked if needed."], ["Months 3–4", "Movement gradually returns. Your clinician can discuss whether to repeat treatment."]], "q": [["What areas are commonly treated?", "Frown lines between the brows, horizontal forehead lines and crow's feet. We also treat neck bands (platysmal bands) and the jawline (Nefertiti lift). Other areas may be discussed at your assessment."], ["What is a Nefertiti lift?", "A Nefertiti lift places small doses of a Neuromodulator along the jawline and into the platysma, the thin muscle in the neck. Relaxing this muscle reduces its downward pull on the lower face and can soften visible neck bands. Your clinician assesses whether it suits you."], ["Who performs the treatment?", "Injectable treatments at Mediworks are performed only by our Naturopathic Doctors, after a consultation."], ["How long does an appointment take?", "About 15–30 minutes for treatment. Your first visit also includes a Naturopathic Aesthetic Consultation."], ["Is there downtime?", "Usually none. For the rest of the day, avoid rubbing the area, strenuous exercise and lying flat."], ["How long does the effect last?", "It varies between people. The effect commonly lasts about three to four months as muscle movement gradually returns."], ["Will I still have natural expression?", "Dosing is planned with you to soften lines while keeping movement. Your clinician will explain what to expect for your face."], ["What are the possible side effects?", "Common effects include temporary redness, small bumps, tenderness or minor bruising at injection sites. Less common risks, such as a temporary drooping eyelid, are reviewed with you before treatment. Neck treatment can rarely cause temporary neck weakness or difficulty swallowing; your clinician reviews this with you."], ["Is it covered by insurance?", "Cosmetic treatments are generally not covered by extended health plans. Naturopathic consultations may be covered, and we offer direct billing; please check your plan."]], "tags": "lines botox dysport wrinkle relaxer", "caution": ["Pregnancy or breastfeeding", "An active skin infection or cold sore in the treatment area", "Certain neuromuscular conditions", "Some medications, including blood thinners, which your clinician will review", "A known allergy to any ingredient"]},
    "therapeutic-botox":{"n": "Therapeutic Neuromodulators", "c": "injectables", "visual": false, "s": "Neuromodulator injections used for chronic migraine and excessive sweating.", "i": "Therapeutic Neuromodulator treatment uses botulinum toxin in a medical dosing pattern for chronic migraine and excessive sweating (hyperhidrosis). Suitability is confirmed at a consultation in South Surrey.", "f": ["About 20–45 min", "Typically every 3–6 months", "Usually none", "Usually 1–4 weeks"], "g": ["Chronic migraine (15 or more headache days a month)", "Tension headaches with tight head, neck and shoulder muscles", "Excessive underarm sweating", "Excessive sweating of the hands or feet"], "caution": ["Pregnancy or breastfeeding", "Neuromuscular conditions such as myasthenia gravis", "A new, sudden or changing headache pattern, which needs medical assessment first", "Sweating that started suddenly or occurs mainly at night, which needs assessment for other causes"], "h": [["Assess", "We review your headache pattern or sweating, your history and past treatments, and confirm it's right for you.", "20 min"], ["Map", "For headaches, we map points across the forehead, temples, back of the head, neck and shoulders. For sweating, a simple starch-iodine test shows exactly where to treat.", "10 min"], ["Comfort", "Underarms need little preparation. Hands and feet are more sensitive, so we use numbing or cooling.", "5–15 min"], ["Treat", "A series of small, shallow injections across the mapped area.", "10–20 min"]], "x": [["Same day", "Mild tenderness at injection sites is common. Avoid rubbing the area."], ["Weeks 1–2", "Sweating may begin to decrease within about one to two weeks."], ["Weeks 2–4", "For migraine, any change in headache frequency is usually assessed over several weeks, and often over two treatment cycles."], ["Months 3–6", "Your clinician reviews your response and discusses whether to repeat treatment."]], "q": [["How is this different from cosmetic treatment?", "The medication is the same, but the dose, number of injection points and placement differ because the goal is medical rather than cosmetic."], ["Who performs the treatment?", "Injectable treatments at Mediworks are performed only by our Naturopathic Doctors, after a consultation."], ["Is it covered by insurance?", "Some extended health plans cover treatment for chronic migraine or hyperhidrosis, sometimes with prior approval. We can provide documentation for your insurer."], ["Does it hurt?", "Most people feel brief pinches. Hands and feet are more sensitive, so numbing or cooling may be used."], ["What are the possible side effects?", "Common effects include tenderness, redness or minor bruising at injection sites. Neck treatment can cause temporary neck stiffness, and hand treatment can cause temporary grip weakness. Your clinician reviews risks with you first."]]},
    "dermal-fillers":{"n": "Dermal Fillers", "c": "injectables", "s": "Hyaluronic acid gel injections that add volume to selected areas of the face.", "i": "Dermal Fillers, including Lip Filler, are hyaluronic acid gels injected to add volume and support to areas such as the lips, cheeks, chin, jawline and under-eyes. Treatment in South Surrey follows a Naturopathic Aesthetic Consultation.", "f": ["About 45–60 min", "Usually 1 visit; repeat as discussed", "Usually 1–3 days of swelling", "Visible right away; settles over about 2 weeks"], "g": ["Hollow cheeks or under-eyes", "A softening jawline or chin", "Lip shape, definition and hydration", "Wanting subtle, reversible results"], "h": [["Consult", "Your clinician assesses facial proportions and discusses your goals, the product and the plan.", "15 min"], ["Numb", "Topical numbing is applied. Most fillers also contain a local anaesthetic.", "15 min"], ["Treat", "Filler is placed with a fine needle or a blunt cannula.", "20–30 min"]], "x": [["Same day", "Change in volume is visible, along with some swelling."], ["Days 2–3", "Swelling and any bruising usually settle."], ["Week 2", "The filler has settled. A review visit is offered if needed."], ["6–18 months", "Filler is gradually broken down by the body. Duration varies by area, product and person."]], "q": [["What areas can be treated?", "Common areas include the cheeks, lips, chin, jawline, temples and under-eyes. Your clinician confirms which areas suit your anatomy."], ["Who performs the treatment?", "Injectable treatments at Mediworks are performed only by our Naturopathic Doctors, after a consultation."], ["How long does filler last?", "It varies. Many hyaluronic acid fillers last about 6 to 18 months, depending on the area, product and individual."], ["Can filler be dissolved?", "Yes. Hyaluronic acid filler can be dissolved with an enzyme called hyaluronidase if needed."], ["What are the possible side effects?", "Swelling, tenderness and bruising are common and usually short-lived. Rare but serious risks, such as filler entering a blood vessel, are explained at your consultation along with how they are managed."], ["Is there downtime?", "Most people return to normal activities the same day. Avoid strenuous exercise, alcohol and pressure on the area for 24 hours."]], "tags": "volume under", "caution": ["Pregnancy or breastfeeding", "An active skin infection or cold sore in the area", "A history of severe allergies or allergy to lidocaine", "Certain autoimmune conditions or blood thinners, which your clinician will review", "An important event within the next two weeks"]},
    "sculptra":{"n": "Sculptra", "c": "injectables", "s": "A collagen-stimulating injectable used to address gradual volume loss.", "i": "Sculptra is an injectable made of poly-L-lactic acid that stimulates the skin's own collagen production over several months. It is used for gradual facial volume loss and is offered in South Surrey after a consultation.", "f": ["About 45 min", "Usually 2–3 sessions, 4–6 weeks apart", "Usually 1–2 days", "Gradual, over about 2–3 months"], "g": ["Overall facial volume loss", "Laxity in the cheeks and temples", "Facial hollowing after Weight Loss", "Crepey skin on the neck and décolletage", "Preferring gradual, natural change"], "h": [["Consult", "Your clinician maps areas of volume loss and plans the number of sessions.", "15 min"], ["Prepare", "The skin is cleansed and numbed.", "15 min"], ["Treat", "The product is injected into the deeper layers of the skin.", "20 min"], ["Massage at home", "You massage the treated area for a few days, as instructed.", "5 min a day for 5 days"]], "x": [["Same day", "Some fullness from the fluid is normal and fades within a few days."], ["Weeks 4–6", "The next session is scheduled if planned."], ["Months 2–3", "Collagen production builds gradually."], ["Ongoing", "Your clinician reviews the change and discusses maintenance."]], "q": [["Why is the change gradual?", "Sculptra works by stimulating collagen, which the body builds over weeks to months, so changes appear gradually rather than straight away."], ["Who performs the treatment?", "Injectable treatments at Mediworks are performed only by our Naturopathic Doctors, after a consultation."], ["Is it a filler?", "It is a collagen stimulator rather than a gel filler. It restores volume indirectly by prompting new collagen."], ["How many sessions will I need?", "Most plans include two to three sessions about four to six weeks apart. Your clinician confirms this at your consultation."], ["What are the possible side effects?", "Swelling, tenderness and bruising are common. Small bumps under the skin can occur; following the massage instructions helps reduce this risk."], ["How long does it last?", "Duration varies. Collagen-stimulating results commonly last longer than hyaluronic acid fillers, and your clinician will discuss what to expect for you."]], "tags": "volume laxity", "caution": ["Pregnancy or breastfeeding", "An active skin infection in the area", "A history of keloid or hypertrophic scarring", "Certain autoimmune conditions, which your clinician will review"]},
    "biofiller":{"n": "Biofiller", "c": "injectables", "s": "A gel made from your own blood plasma, used to add gentle volume.", "i": "A Biofiller is a soft gel made from your own blood plasma, injected to add gentle volume to areas such as the under-eyes. It is an option for people who prefer to avoid synthetic fillers, offered in South Surrey after a consultation.", "f": ["About 60 min", "Usually 1–2 sessions", "Usually 1–2 days", "Over about 2–4 weeks"], "g": ["Under-eye hollows", "Mild volume loss", "Preferring a fully natural option", "Sensitivity to synthetic fillers"], "h": [["Blood draw", "A small blood sample is taken from your arm.", "5 min"], ["Prepare", "Plasma is separated in a centrifuge and gently heated into a gel.", "20 min"], ["Treat", "The gel is placed with a fine cannula.", "20 min"]], "q": [["How long does it last?", "A plasma gel is absorbed by the body more quickly than hyaluronic acid filler, so the effect is generally shorter-lasting. Your clinician will discuss timing for repeat treatment."], ["Who performs the treatment?", "Injectable treatments at Mediworks are performed only by our Naturopathic Doctors, after a consultation."], ["Is it safe if I react to fillers?", "Because it uses your own plasma, it contains no synthetic filler material. Your clinician will review your history to confirm suitability."], ["What are the possible side effects?", "Swelling, tenderness and bruising at the injection and blood draw sites are common and usually short-lived."]], "tags": "volume under dull", "x": [["Same day", "Mild swelling and tenderness are common."], ["Days 1–2", "Swelling usually settles."], ["Weeks 2–4", "Your clinician reviews the area and discusses whether a second session is needed."]], "caution": ["Pregnancy or breastfeeding", "Blood disorders or anticoagulant medications, which your clinician will review", "An active skin infection in the area", "Feeling unwell or having a fever on the day"]},
    "skin-boosters":{"n": "Skin Boosters", "c": "injectables", "s": "Micro-injections of hyaluronic acid that hydrate the skin rather than add volume.", "i": "Skin Boosters are small amounts of fine hyaluronic acid injected across the skin to improve hydration and texture, rather than to add volume. Treatment in South Surrey is usually a short course after a consultation.", "f": ["About 30–45 min", "Usually 2–3 sessions, about 4 weeks apart", "Usually 1–2 days of small bumps", "Gradual, over several weeks"], "g": ["Dehydrated, crepey skin", "Fine lines on the face, neck or hands", "Dull skin that doesn't respond to creams", "Preparing skin for an event"], "h": [["Consult", "Your clinician chooses the treatment areas and product.", "10 min"], ["Numb", "Numbing cream is applied.", "15–20 min"], ["Treat", "Small micro-injections are placed across the area.", "15–20 min"]], "x": [["Days 1–2", "Small bumps and redness usually settle within a day or two."], ["Weeks 2–4", "Hydration changes develop gradually."], ["Weeks 4–8", "Further sessions are scheduled if planned."], ["About 6–12 months", "Your clinician discusses maintenance."]], "q": [["How is this different from filler?", "Skin Boosters are spread thinly through the skin to improve hydration and texture. They are not designed to change shape or add volume."], ["Who performs the treatment?", "Injectable treatments at Mediworks are performed only by our Naturopathic Doctors, after a consultation."], ["Which areas can be treated?", "Commonly the face, neck, décolletage and backs of the hands."], ["What are the possible side effects?", "Small bumps, redness, tenderness and bruising are common and usually settle within a few days."]], "tags": "lines dull", "caution": ["Pregnancy or breastfeeding", "An active skin infection or cold sore in the area", "A history of severe allergies", "An important event within the next week"]},
    "microneedling":{"n": "Microneedling", "c": "regenerative-skin", "s": "A medical pen creates controlled micro-channels to prompt the skin's repair process.", "i": "Microneedling, also called collagen induction therapy, uses fine sterile needles to create controlled micro-channels in the skin. At Mediworks in South Surrey it is used for scarring, texture and pores, and for hyperpigmentation with tranexamic acid and glutathione, usually as a series.", "f": ["About 60 min", "Usually 3–4 sessions, 4–6 weeks apart", "Usually 1–3 days of redness", "Gradual, over several sessions"], "g": ["Acne scars", "Enlarged pores and rough texture", "Fine lines", "Neck and décolletage", "Hyperpigmentation, including melasma and PIH"], "h": [["Numb", "Numbing cream is applied.", "20 min"], ["Treat", "The pen passes over the skin in sections at a set depth.", "20–30 min"], ["Soothe", "A calming serum or mask is applied.", "10 min"]], "x": [["Days 1–2", "Redness similar to a mild sunburn. Avoid makeup for 24 hours."], ["Days 3–5", "Some dryness or light flaking. Use gentle skincare and daily sunscreen."], ["Weeks 4–6", "The next session is booked if planned."], ["Months 3–6", "Collagen remodelling continues gradually after the series."]], "q": [["Does it hurt?", "Numbing cream is applied first. Most people describe a scratchy or vibrating sensation."], ["Is it suitable for darker skin tones?", "Microneedling is generally used across skin tones. Your clinician reviews your skin type and any history of pigmentation first."], ["Can Microneedling help with hyperpigmentation?", "For hyperpigmentation, such as sun spots, melasma or post-inflammatory hyperpigmentation (PIH), we may apply tranexamic acid, glutathione, PRP or Exosomes during Microneedling. Results vary, pigmentation can return, and daily sunscreen is essential. Your clinician will assess your skin and discuss which approach suits you."], ["What are tranexamic acid and glutathione?", "Tranexamic acid is an ingredient used in skin care for uneven pigmentation. Glutathione is an antioxidant. Both are applied to the skin during the session; your clinician confirms the formula."], ["Can it be combined with PRP or Exosomes?", "Yes. PRP or Exosomes can be applied during the session. Your clinician will discuss whether an add-on suits your goals."], ["How many sessions will I need?", "Most plans include three to four sessions about four to six weeks apart. Deeper scarring may need more."], ["What are the possible side effects?", "Redness, swelling, dryness and pinpoint bleeding are common and short-lived. Infection, breakouts and changes in pigmentation are less common and reviewed with you first."]], "tags": "texture", "caution": ["Active acne, cold sores or a skin infection in the area", "Isotretinoin (Accutane) within the past 6 months", "A history of keloid scarring", "Pregnancy", "Blood thinners or a bleeding disorder, which your clinician will review", "A history of blood clots, or allergy to tranexamic acid or glutathione, which your clinician will review"]},
    "exosome-facial":{"n": "Exosomes", "c": "regenerative-skin", "s": "Purasomes Exosomes applied after Microneedling.", "i": "An Exosome Facial applies Purasomes Exosomes by Avari, tiny cell-signalling particles, to the skin right after Microneedling. It is offered in South Surrey as an add-on to support skin recovery and texture.", "f": ["About 60 min", "Usually 1–3 sessions", "Usually 1–2 days of redness", "Varies; gradual over weeks"], "g": ["Dull or tired-looking skin", "Uneven texture", "Neck and décolletage (with Microneedling)", "An add-on to Microneedling"], "q": [["What are Exosomes?", "Exosomes are tiny particles that cells release to send signals to one another. They carry proteins and other molecules but contain no living cells."], ["Where do the Exosomes come from?", "Mediworks uses Purasomes by Avari, purified Exosomes derived from colostrum. They contain no living cells. Your clinician will explain the product and what current research shows."], ["Why are they combined with Microneedling?", "Microneedling creates temporary channels in the skin, which allow the product to reach deeper than it would on intact skin."], ["What are the possible side effects?", "Side effects are mainly those of Microneedling: redness, swelling, dryness and pinpoint bleeding. Research on Exosomes in skin care is still developing."]], "tags": "dull texture", "h": [["Numb", "Numbing cream is applied.", "20 min"], ["Microneedle", "The skin is treated with a medical Microneedling pen.", "20 min"], ["Apply", "The exosome product is applied to the treated skin.", "10 min"]], "x": [["Days 1–2", "Redness and mild tightness are common. Avoid makeup for 24 hours."], ["Days 3–5", "Light dryness may occur. Use gentle skincare and sunscreen."], ["Weeks 4–6", "Your clinician reviews your skin and discusses any further sessions."]], "caution": ["Active acne, cold sores or a skin infection in the area", "Isotretinoin (Accutane) within the past 6 months", "Pregnancy or breastfeeding", "A history of keloid scarring", "Allergy or sensitivity to milk or dairy proteins, as the product is colostrum-derived", "Allergy to any other product ingredient"]},
    "meta-cell-technology":{"n": "Meta Cell Technology", "c": "regenerative-skin", "draft": true, "s": "An injected regenerative skin treatment, discussed at consultation.", "i": "Meta Cell Technology is an injected regenerative skin treatment offered in South Surrey. It is placed into the skin with fine injections and is usually done as a series. Your clinician explains what it contains and whether it suits your skin.", "f": ["About 60 min", "Usually a series", "Usually minimal", "Gradual, over weeks"], "g": ["Texture and tone", "Early laxity", "Fine lines"], "q": [["What does the treatment contain?", "Your clinician will explain the product, how it is prepared and the evidence behind it at your consultation."], ["Who performs the treatment?", "Injectable treatments at Mediworks are performed only by our Naturopathic Doctors, after a consultation."], ["How many sessions will I need?", "It is usually done as a series. The number of sessions depends on your skin and goals."], ["What are the possible side effects?", "As with other skin injections, redness, swelling, tenderness and bruising at injection sites are possible. Your clinician reviews risks with you first."], ["Is it right for me?", "Your clinician assesses your skin and health history at a Naturopathic Aesthetic Consultation and explains the options."]], "tags": "texture laxity", "caution": ["Pregnancy or breastfeeding", "An active skin infection in the area", "Blood thinners or a bleeding disorder, which your clinician will review", "A known allergy to any product ingredient"]},
    "medical-grade-skincare":{"n": "Medical-Grade Skincare", "c": "skincare", "s": "Clinician-selected serums, retinoids and sunscreen.", "i": "Medical-Grade Skincare uses active ingredients such as retinoids, vitamin C, hydroxy acids and sunscreen. At Mediworks in South Surrey, a routine is chosen for your skin type and planned around any in-clinic treatments.", "f": ["About 15 min consultation", "Daily routine", "None", "Gradual, over about 4–12 weeks"], "g": ["Maintaining treatment results", "Pigmentation and uneven tone", "Acne-prone or sensitive skin", "A simpler routine that works"], "h": [["Assess", "Your clinician looks at your skin and current routine.", "10 min"], ["Plan", "A simple morning and evening routine is agreed.", "5 min"], ["Review", "The routine is adjusted as your skin changes.", "At follow-ups"]], "q": [["What makes it medical-grade?", "Medical-grade products typically contain active ingredients at clinically studied concentrations and are selected by a clinician for your skin."], ["Can I use it with my treatments?", "Yes. Your routine is planned around in-clinic treatments, including when to pause certain actives before and after a procedure."], ["Where can I buy it?", "Products are available at the clinic. Ask us about ordering between visits."], ["What if my skin reacts?", "Mild dryness or sensitivity can happen when starting actives. Contact the clinic if irritation persists so your routine can be adjusted."]], "tags": "lines dull texture laxity", "x": [["Weeks 1–2", "Some actives, such as retinoids, can cause mild dryness or irritation as the skin adjusts."], ["Weeks 4–12", "Changes in tone and texture develop gradually with consistent use."], ["Ongoing", "Your routine is reviewed at follow-up visits."]], "caution": ["Pregnancy or breastfeeding, as some ingredients such as retinoids are not recommended", "Very sensitive skin or eczema in the area", "A known allergy to any ingredient", "Recent procedures, before which some actives need to be paused"]},
    "prp-hair-restoration":{"caution": ["Platelet disorders, or blood thinners that raise bleeding risk", "An infection at the treatment site, or feeling unwell on the day", "Active cancer or current cancer treatment", "Some autoimmune or inflammatory conditions, which your clinician will review", "Pregnancy or breastfeeding"], "n": "PRP / PRF for Hair", "c": "hair", "s": "Platelet concentrates from your own blood, injected into thinning areas of the scalp.", "i": "PRP for hair uses Platelet-Rich Plasma (PRP) or Platelet-Rich Fibrin (PRF) prepared from your own blood and injected into thinning areas of the scalp. It is a Hair Loss treatment for early to moderate thinning in men and women, usually given as a series at our South Surrey clinic.", "f": ["About 60 min", "Usually 3 sessions, about 4 weeks apart", "Usually minimal", "Gradual, often assessed at 3–6 months"], "g": ["Early to moderate thinning in men or women", "A widening part or receding hairline", "Shedding after stress, illness or pregnancy", "Support alongside other hair treatments"], "h": [["Blood draw", "A small sample is taken from your arm, similar to a routine lab test.", "5 min"], ["Prepare", "A centrifuge concentrates the platelets in a sterile, single-use kit.", "15 min"], ["Comfort", "The scalp is numbed or cooled.", "15 min"], ["Treat", "PRP or PRF is placed across areas of thinning with fine micro-injections.", "20 min"]], "x": [["Day 1", "Mild tenderness is common. You can usually wash your hair the next day."], ["Weeks 4–8", "Further sessions are completed as planned."], ["Months 3–6", "Your clinician reviews progress, often with comparison photos."], ["Ongoing", "Maintenance is discussed, often once or twice a year."]], "q": [["Does it hurt?", "Most people describe pressure rather than pain. The scalp is numbed or cooled first, and most return to work the same day."], ["How many sessions will I need?", "Most plans start with three sessions about a month apart, followed by maintenance if you choose."], ["What is the difference between PRP and PRF?", "PRF is spun more gently and without additives, so it releases growth factors more slowly. Your clinician recommends one based on your hair and goals."], ["Who is it suitable for?", "It is generally considered for early to moderate thinning where hair is still present in the area. An assessment, sometimes with bloodwork, comes first."], ["What are the possible side effects?", "Tenderness, mild swelling, bruising and a brief headache are possible. Infection is rare."]]},
    "exosome-hair-therapy":{"n": "Exosome Hair Therapy", "c": "hair", "s": "Purasomes Exosomes applied to the scalp, with no blood draw.", "i": "Exosome hair therapy applies Purasomes Exosomes by Avari to the scalp, often with Microneedling. It does not need a blood draw and is offered in South Surrey as part of a plan for thinning hair.", "f": ["About 45–60 min", "Usually 1–3 sessions", "Usually minimal", "Gradual, often assessed at 3–6 months"], "g": ["Thinning in men or women", "An option alongside PRP or medication", "When a blood draw is not suitable"], "q": [["Can it be combined with PRP?", "Yes. Some plans combine Exosomes with PRP or PRF. Your clinician will discuss whether that suits you."], ["Where do the Exosomes come from?", "Mediworks uses Purasomes by Avari, purified Exosomes derived from colostrum. They contain no living cells. Your clinician will explain the product and what current research shows."], ["What does the evidence say?", "Research on Exosomes for hair is early and still developing. Your clinician will explain what is currently known."], ["What are the possible side effects?", "Redness, tenderness and mild swelling of the scalp are possible and usually short-lived."]], "h": [["Assess", "Your clinician reviews your scalp and treatment plan.", "10 min"], ["Prepare", "The scalp is cleansed and may be numbed.", "15 min"], ["Treat", "Exosomes are applied with Microneedling or placed with fine injections.", "20–30 min"]], "x": [["Day 1", "Mild redness or tenderness is common."], ["Weeks 4–8", "Further sessions are completed if planned."], ["Months 3–6", "Your clinician reviews progress."]], "caution": ["An active scalp infection or skin condition in the area", "Pregnancy or breastfeeding", "Active cancer or current cancer treatment", "Allergy or sensitivity to milk or dairy proteins, as the product is colostrum-derived", "Allergy to any other product ingredient"]},
    "alopecia-injections":{"n": "Corticosteroid Injections for Alopecia", "c": "hair", "s": "Small corticosteroid injections for patchy Hair Loss.", "i": "Corticosteroid injections are a common treatment for Alopecia Areata, a condition that causes patchy Hair Loss. Small amounts of medication are injected into affected patches every four to six weeks at our South Surrey clinic.", "f": ["About 15–30 min", "Typically every 4–6 weeks", "Usually none", "Often assessed over 6–12 weeks"], "g": ["Round, patchy Hair Loss", "Patches in the beard or brows", "Small, localized areas of loss"], "q": [["Is this the same as PRP?", "No. These injections reduce the immune reaction behind patchy Hair Loss, while PRP is used for pattern thinning."], ["How many treatments will I need?", "It varies. Injections are usually repeated every four to six weeks and reviewed regularly."], ["What are the possible side effects?", "Temporary tenderness is common. A small, usually temporary dip in the skin (atrophy) or lightening of the skin at the injection site can occur."], ["Will the Hair Loss come back?", "Alopecia Areata can come and go. Your clinician will discuss what to expect and how to monitor it."]], "h": [["Assess", "Your clinician examines the patches and confirms the diagnosis.", "10 min"], ["Prepare", "The skin is cleansed.", "5 min"], ["Treat", "Small injections are placed into each patch.", "5–15 min"]], "x": [["Same day", "Mild tenderness or pinpoint bleeding may occur."], ["Weeks 4–6", "Patches are reviewed and treatment is repeated if needed."], ["Months 2–3", "Your clinician assesses the response and adjusts the plan."]], "caution": ["An infection in the treatment area", "Pregnancy or breastfeeding", "Diabetes or glaucoma, which your clinician will review", "Hair Loss that has not yet been assessed or diagnosed"]},
    "ultrasound-guided-prp":{"caution": ["Platelet disorders, or blood thinners that raise bleeding risk", "An infection at the treatment site, or feeling unwell on the day", "Active cancer or current cancer treatment", "Some autoimmune or inflammatory conditions, which your clinician will review", "Pregnancy or breastfeeding"], "n": "Ultrasound-Guided PRP", "c": "joint-arthritis", "s": "PRP injections placed into tendons, ligaments or joints with ultrasound guidance.", "i": "Ultrasound-guided PRP uses real-time imaging to place Platelet-Rich Plasma from your own blood into an injured tendon, ligament or joint. It is offered at our South Surrey clinic after an assessment of the area.", "f": ["About 60 min", "Usually 1–3 sessions", "Usually 2–3 days of soreness", "Gradual, often over 4–12 weeks"], "g": ["Tendon problems such as tennis elbow, Achilles or rotator cuff", "Knee, hip or shoulder Osteoarthritis", "Ligament sprains that have been slow to heal", "Exploring options before surgery"], "h": [["Assess", "An examination and ultrasound scan of the area.", "15 min"], ["Blood draw", "A sample is spun to concentrate the platelets in a sterile, single-use kit.", "20 min"], ["Inject", "The skin is numbed and PRP is placed under ultrasound guidance.", "15 min"], ["Plan recovery", "A plan for a gradual return to activity, often with physiotherapy.", "Ongoing"]], "x": [["Days 1–3", "Soreness is common as the body responds. Rest the area as advised."], ["Weeks 2–6", "Gradual return to activity, often with guided exercises."], ["Weeks 6–12", "Your clinician reviews progress and discusses whether another session is needed."]], "q": [["Why use ultrasound?", "Ultrasound shows the tissue and the needle in real time, which helps place the injection in the intended area."], ["Can I take anti-inflammatories?", "Anti-inflammatory medication may interfere with the healing response PRP relies on. Ask your clinician what to use for pain before and after."], ["How many sessions will I need?", "Often one to three, depending on the condition and your response."], ["Is it an alternative to surgery?", "For some conditions, PRP may be considered before surgery. Your clinician will discuss all options, including referral where appropriate."], ["What are the possible side effects?", "Soreness, swelling and bruising are common for a few days. Infection and nerve irritation are rare."]]},
    "knee-oa-injections":{"n": "Hyaluronic Acid Knee Injections", "c": "joint-arthritis", "s": "Hyaluronic acid injections for an osteoarthritic knee.", "i": "Hyaluronic acid knee injections, also called viscosupplements, add hyaluronic acid to the knee joint to support cushioning and lubrication. They are used for Knee Osteoarthritis at our South Surrey clinic.", "f": ["About 20–30 min", "Often 1 injection; repeat as discussed", "Usually 1–2 days", "Often over 2–6 weeks"], "g": ["Knee Osteoarthritis", "Pain or stiffness with walking or stairs", "Options alongside exercise and Weight Management"], "q": [["Which products are used?", "Several hyaluronic acid products are available, including one that also contains a corticosteroid. Your clinician will recommend one at your assessment."], ["How long does it last?", "It varies. Some people notice a benefit for several months. Your clinician will discuss when to review."], ["What are the possible side effects?", "Temporary pain, swelling or warmth in the knee are the most common. Infection is rare."], ["Is it covered by insurance?", "Some extended health plans cover viscosupplements, sometimes with prior approval. Please check your plan."]], "h": [["Assess", "Your clinician examines the knee and reviews imaging if available.", "10 min"], ["Prepare", "The skin is cleansed and may be numbed.", "5 min"], ["Inject", "Hyaluronic acid is injected into the joint.", "5–10 min"]], "x": [["Days 1–2", "Mild soreness or swelling is common. Avoid strenuous activity for about 48 hours."], ["Weeks 2–6", "Any change in pain and stiffness is usually noticed gradually."], ["6–12 months", "Your clinician reviews the knee and discusses whether to repeat."]], "caution": ["An infection in or around the knee", "Allergy to hyaluronic acid products or bird proteins, depending on the product", "Significant swelling of the knee, which needs assessment first", "Pregnancy or breastfeeding"]},
    "prolotherapy":{"n": "Prolotherapy", "c": "joint-arthritis", "s": "Dextrose injections where ligaments and tendons attach to bone.", "i": "Prolotherapy is an injection treatment for chronic ligament and tendon pain. A solution, usually concentrated dextrose, is injected where these tissues attach to bone. It is usually done as a series at our South Surrey clinic.", "f": ["About 30–45 min", "Usually 3–6 sessions, 4–6 weeks apart", "Usually 1–3 days of soreness", "Gradual, often over several sessions"], "g": ["Chronic back, neck or joint pain", "Joints that feel loose or unstable", "Old sprains that have been slow to settle"], "q": [["How is it different from PRP?", "Both are intended to prompt a healing response. Prolotherapy usually uses a dextrose solution, while PRP uses platelets from your own blood."], ["Does it hurt?", "The skin is numbed first. Most people feel pressure and some soreness afterwards."], ["Can I take anti-inflammatories?", "Anti-inflammatory medication may interfere with the intended response. Ask your clinician what to use for pain."], ["What are the possible side effects?", "Soreness, stiffness, swelling and bruising are common. Infection and nerve irritation are rare."]], "h": [["Assess", "Your clinician examines the area and identifies the treatment points.", "15 min"], ["Prepare", "The skin is cleansed and numbed.", "5 min"], ["Inject", "Several small injections are placed at the attachment points.", "15–20 min"]], "x": [["Days 1–3", "Soreness and stiffness are common. Gentle movement is encouraged."], ["Weeks 4–6", "The next session is booked if planned."], ["After several sessions", "Your clinician reviews progress and adjusts the plan."]], "caution": ["An infection at the treatment site", "Blood thinners or a bleeding disorder, which your clinician will review", "Pregnancy", "Allergy to any ingredient, including local anaesthetic"]},
    "prp-for-pain":{"caution": ["Platelet disorders, or blood thinners that raise bleeding risk", "An infection at the treatment site, or feeling unwell on the day", "Active cancer or current cancer treatment", "Some autoimmune or inflammatory conditions, which your clinician will review", "Pregnancy or breastfeeding"], "n": "PRP for Pain", "c": "muscle-soft-tissue", "s": "Platelet-Rich Plasma injections for tendons, ligaments, muscles and joints.", "i": "PRP for pain uses Platelet-Rich Plasma from your own blood, injected into injured or degenerating tendons, ligaments, muscles or joints. It is offered at our South Surrey clinic after an assessment, usually as one to three sessions.", "f": ["About 45–60 min", "Usually 1–3 sessions", "Usually 2–3 days of soreness", "Gradual, often over 4–12 weeks"], "g": ["Chronic tendon pain", "Osteoarthritis", "Ligament and muscle injuries", "Plantar fasciitis"], "h": [["Assess", "Your clinician examines the area and reviews any imaging.", "15 min"], ["Blood draw", "A sample is spun to concentrate the platelets.", "20 min"], ["Inject", "The skin is numbed and PRP is injected into the area.", "15 min"], ["Plan recovery", "Guidance on activity and rehabilitation.", "Ongoing"]], "x": [["Days 1–3", "Soreness is common as the body responds."], ["Weeks 2–6", "Gradual return to activity, often with exercises or physiotherapy."], ["Weeks 6–12", "Your clinician reviews progress and discusses next steps."]], "q": [["How is it different from ultrasound-guided PRP?", "The treatment is the same. Ultrasound guidance is used when the target tissue is small or deep and imaging helps placement."], ["Can I take anti-inflammatories?", "Anti-inflammatory medication may interfere with PRP's intended effect. Ask your clinician what to use for pain."], ["How many sessions will I need?", "Often one to three, depending on the condition and your response."], ["What are the possible side effects?", "Soreness, swelling and bruising are common for a few days. Infection is rare."]]},
    "trigger-point-injections":{"n": "Trigger Point Injections", "c": "muscle-soft-tissue", "s": "Small injections into tight, tender muscle knots.", "i": "Trigger Point Injections place a small amount of local anaesthetic into tight, tender knots in muscle, called trigger points. They are used for muscle pain in the neck, shoulders and back at our South Surrey clinic.", "f": ["About 15–30 min", "As needed", "Usually none to 1 day", "Varies; some notice a change the same day"], "g": ["Neck and shoulder muscle tension", "Tension-type headaches linked to neck muscles", "Back pain from muscle knots"], "h": [["Assess", "Your clinician locates the trigger points by examination.", "10 min"], ["Prepare", "The skin is cleansed.", "2 min"], ["Inject", "A small amount of local anaesthetic is injected into each point.", "5–15 min"]], "x": [["Same day", "Mild soreness at injection sites is common. Gentle stretching is usually recommended."], ["Days 1–2", "Any soreness usually settles."], ["Follow-up", "Your clinician reviews your response and discusses a home stretching plan."]], "q": [["What is a trigger point?", "A small, tender area of tight muscle that can cause local pain and pain felt elsewhere, such as from the shoulders into the head."], ["How quickly will I notice a difference?", "It varies. Some people notice a change the same day, while others need more than one session."], ["What are the possible side effects?", "Soreness, bruising and light-headedness are possible. Rare risks depend on the area treated and are reviewed with you first."]], "caution": ["An infection at the treatment site", "Blood thinners or a bleeding disorder", "Allergy to local anaesthetic", "Pregnancy, which your clinician will review"]},
    "glp1-support":{"n": "GLP-1 Support", "c": "weight-metabolic", "s": "Medically supervised Weight Loss, with GLP-1 medication where appropriate.", "i": "GLP-1 medications are prescription treatments that reduce appetite and support blood sugar control. At Mediworks in South Surrey, medically supervised GLP-1 Weight Loss care includes an assessment, prescribing where appropriate, nutrition and strength guidance, and regular monitoring.", "f": ["About 60 min first visit", "Ongoing, with regular check-ins", "None", "Varies; reviewed at each check-in"], "g": ["Weight that has not responded to diet and exercise", "Insulin Resistance or prediabetes", "Wanting medical supervision", "Support for muscle and skin during Weight Loss"], "h": [["Assess", "Health history, bloodwork and Body Composition.", "60 min"], ["Plan", "Medication if appropriate, plus nutrition and strength guidance.", "Visit 2"], ["Monitor", "Regular check-ins to review progress, side effects and muscle.", "Every 2–4 weeks"], ["Maintain", "A plan for the longer term, including if and when medication is reduced.", "Ongoing"]], "q": [["Who prescribes the medication?", "Prescriptions are provided by a clinician with the appropriate prescribing authority. Our team includes a Medical Doctor and a Nurse Practitioner."], ["Am I eligible?", "Eligibility depends on your health history, current health and medications. It is assessed at your first visit."], ["What are the common side effects?", "Nausea, constipation, diarrhoea and reduced appetite are common, especially when starting or increasing the dose. Less common but serious risks are reviewed with you before starting."], ["Is it covered by insurance?", "Naturopathic visits may be covered by extended health plans, and we offer direct billing. Coverage for the medication varies by plan and by reason for treatment, so please check with your insurer."]], "x": [["Before you start", "Health history, eligibility and bloodwork, plus a baseline Styku 3D Body Scan so muscle can be tracked as well as weight."], ["Weeks 1–4", "Medication starts at a low dose and is increased gradually. Nausea and fullness are most common early on. You get protein, fluid and strength-training guidance."], ["Months 1–3", "Check-ins every 2–4 weeks to review appetite, side effects, nutrition and strength."], ["Around month 6", "A repeat body scan checks fat lost against muscle kept. Bloodwork is reviewed and the dose adjusted."], ["Month 12 and beyond", "A maintenance plan: continue, reduce or stop the medication, with a plan to keep your habits and keep monitoring if you stop."]], "caution": ["Pregnancy, planning a pregnancy or breastfeeding", "A personal or family history of medullary thyroid cancer or MEN2", "A history of pancreatitis", "Significant gallbladder or kidney disease, which your clinician will review", "A current or past eating disorder"]},
    "slimworks":{"n": "Slimworks Protocol", "c": "weight-metabolic", "s": "A structured Weight Management protocol with coaching.", "i": "Slimworks is a Naturopathic Weight Management protocol at Mediworks in South Surrey. It combines a structured eating plan with regular coaching check-ins and Body Composition tracking, with a focus on habits that can be maintained.", "f": ["About 45 min first visit", "Usually several weeks", "None", "Reviewed at each check-in"], "g": ["A clear, structured plan", "Regular accountability", "Building habits that can be maintained"], "q": [["Is it safe?", "The protocol is tailored to your health history and medications, and supervised by a Naturopathic Doctor."], ["How much weight will I lose?", "It varies between people. Progress is tracked with Body Composition measurements rather than weight alone."], ["Do I need medication?", "No. Slimworks is a nutrition and coaching protocol. If medication may be relevant, it can be discussed separately."], ["What happens after the protocol?", "You receive a plan for transitioning to everyday eating and maintaining your habits."]], "h": [["Assess", "Health history, goals and Body Composition.", "45 min"], ["Plan", "A structured eating plan tailored to your health and medications.", "Visit 1"], ["Coach", "Regular check-ins to review progress and troubleshoot.", "Weekly or as planned"], ["Transition", "A plan for moving from the structured phase to everyday eating.", "End of protocol"]], "x": [["Weeks 1–2", "Getting used to the eating plan. Questions are reviewed at check-ins."], ["During the protocol", "Regular check-ins and Body Composition tracking."], ["After", "A maintenance plan to support the habits you have built."]], "caution": ["Pregnancy or breastfeeding", "Diabetes or blood pressure medications that may need adjusting", "A current or past eating disorder", "Kidney or liver disease, which your clinician will review"]},
    "insulin-resistance":{"n": "Insulin Resistance Treatment", "c": "weight-metabolic", "s": "Testing and care for Insulin Resistance.", "i": "Insulin Resistance is when the body's cells respond less to insulin, so more is needed to keep blood sugar in range. At Mediworks in South Surrey, care starts with testing, followed by a plan and repeat testing.", "f": ["Bloodwork + consultation", "Re-test about every 3 months", "None", "Reviewed with repeat testing"], "g": ["Weight gain around the middle", "Energy dips or cravings after meals", "A family history of type 2 diabetes", "PCOS or prediabetes"], "h": [["Test", "Fasting bloodwork, including insulin and glucose.", "15 min"], ["Review", "Your results explained in plain language.", "30 min"], ["Plan", "Nutrition, activity, sleep and, where appropriate, supplements or medication.", "Ongoing"], ["Re-test", "Repeat bloodwork to track change.", "About 3 months"]], "q": [["What is HOMA-IR?", "A score calculated from fasting insulin and glucose that estimates Insulin Resistance."], ["Is Insulin Resistance the same as diabetes?", "No. Insulin Resistance can be present for years before blood sugar rises into the prediabetes or diabetes range."], ["Do I need medication?", "Not always. Many plans focus on nutrition, activity and sleep. Medication may be discussed where appropriate."], ["Will my family doctor be informed?", "With your consent, we can share results with your family doctor."]], "x": [["Week 1", "Fasting bloodwork and a results review."], ["Months 1–3", "Working through your plan, with check-ins as needed."], ["Month 3", "Repeat testing and a review of the plan."]], "caution": ["Diabetes medications that may need adjusting", "Pregnancy", "Very high blood sugar readings, which need prompt medical review"]},
    "guided-fasting":{"n": "Fasting Protocols", "c": "weight-metabolic", "s": "Structured fasting, guided by a Naturopathic Doctor.", "i": "Fasting protocols are structured ways of timing when you eat, from daily time-restricted eating to occasional longer fasts. At Mediworks in South Surrey, the approach is tailored to your health, medications and goals.", "f": ["About 45 min consultation", "Ongoing", "None", "Reviewed at follow-ups"], "g": ["Metabolic health", "Weight Management", "Structure and support"], "q": [["Is fasting safe with medication?", "Some medications, especially for diabetes or blood pressure, may need adjusting. That is why the plan is made with you."], ["Who should not fast?", "Fasting is not recommended during pregnancy or breastfeeding, or with a history of an eating disorder. Your clinician reviews other conditions."], ["Which type of fasting is best?", "It depends on your health, schedule and goals. Many people start with time-restricted eating."]], "h": [["Assess", "Health history, medications and goals.", "30 min"], ["Plan", "A fasting approach suited to you, with guidance on protein and hydration.", "15 min"], ["Review", "Check-ins to adjust the plan.", "As planned"]], "x": [["Weeks 1–2", "Starting gradually. Hunger and energy changes are common early on."], ["Weeks 2–8", "Check-ins to review how you are feeling and adjust."], ["Ongoing", "Bloodwork or Body Composition may be repeated to track change."]], "caution": ["Pregnancy or breastfeeding", "A current or past eating disorder", "Diabetes or blood pressure medications that may need adjusting", "Being underweight", "Under 18 years of age"]},
    "prolon":{"n": "Prolon FMD", "c": "weight-metabolic", "s": "A five-day meal plan designed to mimic fasting.", "i": "Prolon is a pre-packaged, five-day, plant-based meal plan designed to mimic some effects of fasting while you still eat. At Mediworks in South Surrey, your clinician reviews whether it suits you and supports you through it.", "f": ["About 30 min consultation", "5 days, repeated as advised", "None", "Reviewed after each cycle"], "g": ["Interest in fasting with food", "Metabolic health goals", "Healthy ageing goals"], "h": [["Assess", "Your clinician reviews your health and medications.", "20 min"], ["Prepare", "Guidance on timing, hydration and what to expect.", "10 min"], ["Support", "Check-ins during and after the five days.", "As planned"]], "x": [["Days 1–3", "Hunger, low energy and headaches are common as the body adjusts."], ["Days 4–5", "Many people find hunger eases."], ["Day 6", "A gradual return to normal eating, as guided."]], "q": [["Who should not use it?", "It is not suitable during pregnancy or breastfeeding, with a history of eating disorders, or for people who are underweight. Your clinician reviews other conditions and medications."], ["How often is it repeated?", "Your clinician advises on timing. It is often repeated a few times a year."], ["Can I exercise during the five days?", "Light activity is usually fine. Strenuous exercise is best avoided."]], "caution": ["Pregnancy or breastfeeding", "A current or past eating disorder", "Being underweight", "Diabetes or blood pressure medications that may need adjusting", "Nut or soy allergies, depending on the product contents"]},
    "styku-scan":{"n": "Styku 3D Body Scan", "c": "body-composition", "s": "A contact-free 3D scan of body shape and estimated composition.", "i": "A Styku scan is a quick, contact-free 3D body scan. It measures body shape and circumferences and estimates Body Composition, so changes can be tracked over time at our South Surrey clinic.", "f": ["About 10 min", "Often repeated every 4–12 weeks", "None", "Report reviewed at the visit"], "g": ["Tracking change during a weight protocol", "Monitoring muscle during GLP-1 care", "Seeing changes in shape"], "h": [["Change", "Wear fitted clothing.", "2 min"], ["Scan", "Stand still on a slowly rotating platform.", "1 min"], ["Review", "Your clinician goes through the report with you.", "10 min"]], "q": [["Does it use radiation?", "No. Styku uses infrared depth sensors and does not use X-rays."], ["How accurate is it?", "It gives precise shape and circumference measurements. Body fat is an estimate, which is most useful for tracking change over time. For detailed Body Composition and bone density, a DEXA Scan may be recommended."], ["How do I prepare?", "Wear fitted clothing, such as athletic wear, and try to scan at a similar time of day for repeat scans."]], "caution": ["Pregnancy, as Body Composition estimates are not designed for it"]},
    "dexa-scan":{"n": "DEXA Scan", "c": "body-composition", "s": "A low-dose scan of body fat, lean muscle and bone density.", "i": "A DEXA Scan is a low-dose X-ray scan that measures body fat, lean muscle and bone density, region by region. Any of our Naturopathic Doctors can refer you; the scan is done at our partner clinic, BodyComp Imaging, and your ND reviews the results with you in South Surrey.", "f": ["About 15 min scan", "Yearly or as advised", "None", "Report usually within days"], "g": ["Detailed Body Composition", "Bone health", "Tracking muscle during Weight Loss or with age"], "q": [["Where is it done?", "At our partner clinic, <a class=\"link\" href=\"https://www.bodycomp.ca\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">BodyComp Imaging ↗</a>, which has locations in Vancouver (West Broadway) and Richmond (Richmond Oval). Any of our Naturopathic Doctors can refer you, and your ND reviews the results with you."], ["How much radiation is involved?", "DEXA uses a very low dose of X-rays, much lower than many other X-ray tests."], ["How is it different from a Styku scan?", "DEXA measures fat, lean tissue and bone directly. Styku is a contact-free 3D scan that measures shape and estimates body fat."]], "h": [["Refer", "Your Naturopathic Doctor refers you to BodyComp Imaging, our partner clinic.", "Before"], ["Scan", "You lie still on a padded table while the scanner arm passes over you.", "About 10–15 min"], ["Review", "Your clinician goes through the report with you.", "20 min"]], "x": [["Before", "Wear clothing without metal and avoid calcium supplements on the day, unless told otherwise."], ["After", "BodyComp Imaging sends the report to Mediworks, usually within days."], ["Review", "Your results are explained and used to plan or adjust your care."]], "caution": ["Pregnancy or possible pregnancy", "A recent barium or contrast test, which can affect results"]},
    "bhrt":{"n": "Bioidentical Hormones (BHRT)", "c": "hormones", "s": "Hormone care for Perimenopause and Menopause.", "i": "Bioidentical Hormone Replacement Therapy (BHRT) uses hormones with the same molecular structure as those the body makes. As part of Menopause and Perimenopause care at Mediworks in South Surrey, a plan is considered after testing and a review of your symptoms and history.", "f": ["About 60 min first visit", "Ongoing, with check-ins", "None", "Often reviewed over weeks to 3 months"], "g": ["Hot flashes and night sweats", "Poor sleep, low mood or brain fog", "Low libido", "Irregular periods in Perimenopause"], "q": [["Is BHRT safe?", "It depends on your personal and family history. Your clinician reviews risks and benefits with you before starting and monitors you over time."], ["What forms are available?", "Options can include creams, gels, patches and capsules. Your clinician will discuss which suits you."], ["Are Bioidentical Hormones the same as compounded hormones?", "Not necessarily. Some Bioidentical Hormones are approved products, while others are compounded by a pharmacy. Your clinician will explain the difference."], ["Who prescribes it?", "Prescriptions are provided by a clinician with the appropriate prescribing authority."]], "h": [["Assess", "A detailed review of symptoms, personal and family history.", "60 min"], ["Test", "Bloodwork or other Hormone Testing, as appropriate.", "As needed"], ["Plan", "Options, risks and benefits are discussed. A plan is agreed if appropriate.", "Follow-up visit"], ["Review", "Regular check-ins to adjust the dose and form.", "Ongoing"]], "x": [["Weeks 1–4", "Some people notice early changes. Mild side effects, such as breast tenderness or spotting, can occur."], ["Months 1–3", "Your clinician reviews symptoms and adjusts the plan."], ["Ongoing", "Regular review, including whether to continue treatment."]], "caution": ["A personal history of breast or uterine cancer", "A history of blood clots or stroke", "Unexplained vaginal bleeding, which needs assessment first", "Active liver disease", "Pregnancy"]},
    "trt":{"n": "Testosterone Replacement Therapy (TRT)", "c": "hormones", "s": "A virtual, medically supervised protocol for men with confirmed low Testosterone.", "i": "Testosterone Replacement Therapy (TRT) is a medical treatment for men with confirmed low Testosterone. The Mediworks TRT protocol starts with bloodwork at LifeLabs, followed by a virtual Initial Consultation with Dr. Birpal Pannu, MD or Stephen Martin, NP, to review your results and decide whether TRT is right for you.", "f": ["Virtual visits", "12-month protocol", "None", "Reviewed over about 3–12 weeks"], "g": ["Low energy and motivation", "Low libido", "Loss of muscle or strength", "Low mood or poor focus"], "h": [["Bloodwork first", "Comprehensive blood work at LifeLabs to measure your Testosterone and safety markers.", "Step 1"], ["Initial Consultation", "A virtual visit where your practitioner reviews your symptoms and results with you and decides whether TRT is right for you.", "Step 2"], ["Start your plan", "A personalized treatment plan, with your prescription sent directly to your pharmacy.", "Step 3"], ["Follow-up and monitoring", "Regular virtual check-ins and lab testing throughout the year, with your plan adjusted to your symptoms and blood work.", "Ongoing"], ["Annual renewal", "Review your progress and renew the protocol for the following year.", "Yearly"]], "q": [["Are the consultations virtual?", "Yes. TRT consultations and follow-ups are virtual, so you can join from home. Bloodwork is done at LifeLabs."], ["Will it affect fertility?", "Testosterone Therapy can reduce sperm production. Tell your clinician if you are planning children so options can be discussed."], ["How is Testosterone given?", "At Mediworks, Testosterone is prescribed as an injection only. Your prescription is sent to your pharmacy, and your clinician explains your dose, how often it's given and the monitoring involved."], ["What are the possible side effects?", "These can include acne, fluid retention, a rise in red blood cell count and changes in PSA. Regular bloodwork monitors these."], ["Is it covered by insurance?", "The TRT protocol itself is not eligible for reimbursement through extended health insurance. Your prescription may be covered by your extended health plan."], ["Is the bloodwork covered?", "Most TRT bloodwork is covered by MSP. At your first bloodwork, Bioavailable Testosterone, Vitamin D and PSA are not covered, and you pay LifeLabs directly for those. Follow-up bloodwork is covered by MSP, except PSA, which is checked every 6 months and paid directly to LifeLabs."]], "x": [["Weeks 1–3", "Bloodwork at LifeLabs, then a virtual Initial Consultation to review your symptoms and results and decide whether TRT is appropriate."], ["Months 1–3", "If treatment starts, follow-up and repeat bloodwork to check levels and safety markers."], ["Ongoing", "Regular virtual check-ins and an annual review."]], "caution": ["Prostate or breast cancer, or an abnormal PSA result", "Planning children in the near future", "Untreated sleep apnoea", "A high red blood cell count", "A recent heart attack or stroke"]},
    "vo2-max":{"n": "VO2 Max Testing", "c": "cardio-fitness", "s": "A measure of cardiorespiratory fitness, with personal training zones.", "i": "A VO2 max test measures the maximum amount of oxygen your body can use during exercise. At Mediworks in South Surrey, it is used to set personal heart rate training zones and track fitness over time as part of longevity care.", "f": ["About 45–60 min", "Often re-tested every 6–12 months", "None", "Same-day results review"], "g": ["Healthy ageing goals", "Active people and athletes", "Setting training zones", "Tracking fitness over time"], "h": [["Prepare", "Wear exercise clothes and avoid a heavy meal beforehand.", "Before"], ["Test", "A progressive exercise test while your breathing is measured through a mask.", "15–20 min"], ["Review", "Your score, a comparison for your age and your training zones.", "20 min"]], "q": [["Is it hard?", "It builds to your maximum effort, but only for a few minutes. You can stop at any time."], ["Why does VO2 max matter?", "Higher cardiorespiratory fitness is associated with better long-term health in research studies. It is also a useful measure to track."], ["Who should not do the test?", "People with certain heart or lung conditions may need medical clearance first. Your clinician will review your health history."]], "caution": ["Chest pain, recent heart events or uncontrolled high blood pressure", "Unstable asthma or lung disease", "A recent injury that limits exercise", "Pregnancy, which your clinician will review"]},
"rmr":{"n": "Resting Metabolic Rate (RMR)", "c": "body-composition", "s": "A breathing test that measures how many calories your body burns at rest.", "i": "A resting metabolic rate (RMR) test measures the oxygen you use while lying quietly, to estimate how many calories your body burns at rest. At Mediworks in South Surrey, it is used to set calorie and protein targets for Weight Loss and to check that your metabolism holds up as you lose weight.", "f": ["About 15–20 min", "Usually at the start and end of a protocol", "None", "Results reviewed the same day"], "g": ["Setting calorie targets for Weight Loss", "Checking metabolism during GLP-1 care", "Understanding a Weight Loss plateau", "Healthy ageing baselines"], "h": [["Prepare", "Come fasted, and avoid caffeine and exercise beforehand.", "Before"], ["Rest", "Lie quietly while your breathing is measured through a mask or mouthpiece.", "10–15 min"], ["Review", "Your calories at rest, compared with what is expected for your size and age.", "10 min"]], "q": [["Why measure RMR instead of using a calculator?", "Online formulas estimate RMR from height, weight and age, and can be off for many people. Measuring it gives a target based on your own metabolism."], ["How do I prepare?", "Usually no food for 4 hours, no caffeine or nicotine that morning, and no hard exercise the day before. Your clinic will confirm the details."], ["How often is it repeated?", "Often at the start and end of a Weight Loss Protocol, or if your weight loss stalls."]], "caution": ["A cold, fever or blocked nose on the day, as these can affect the reading", "Pregnancy, which your clinician will review"]},
"pillcheck":{"n": "Pillcheck Drug Response Test", "c": "genetics", "s": "A clinician-ordered pharmacogenomic test showing how your genes affect your response to common medications.", "i": "Pillcheck, from GeneYouIn, is a pharmacogenomic test processed in a Canadian lab. It shows how your genes affect the way you process common medications, and comes with a pharmacist's written opinion you can share with your family doctor. At Mediworks in South Surrey, it is offered on its own or as an add-on to the Longevity Protocol.", "f": ["Cheek swab", "Once, with free re-analysis", "None", "Results in about 1–2 weeks"], "g": ["Taking several medications", "Side effects or a medication that did not work", "Starting antidepressants, pain medication, statins or blood thinners", "Longevity planning"], "h": [["Review", "Your clinician reviews your medications and decides whether testing will help.", "At your visit"], ["Swab", "A cheek swab, sent to a Canadian lab.", "5 min"], ["Results", "A report with a pharmacist's opinion, shared with you and your prescriber.", "1–2 weeks"]], "q": [["Will it tell me which medication to take?", "It shows how your genes may affect your response to many medications. Your prescriber uses it with your history and other factors; never change a medication on your own."], ["Is it covered?", "MSP and PharmaCare do not cover pharmacogenomic tests. Some extended health plans do, so check your plan."], ["Is this the same as SelfDecode's medication report?", "No. Pillcheck is a dedicated clinical test with a pharmacist's interpretation. SelfDecode's report is for general insight only."]], "caution": ["Do not stop or change any medication based on the results without talking to your prescriber", "A recent blood transfusion or a bone marrow transplant can affect results"]},
    "truage":{"n": "TruAge + TruHealth Epigenetic Test", "c": "longevity-testing", "s": "A finger-prick test that estimates biological age from DNA methylation.", "i": "TruAge + TruHealth by TruDiagnostic estimates your biological age and pace of aging from chemical tags on your DNA, with additional health-related estimates. At Mediworks in South Surrey, results are reviewed with your clinician and re-tested over time.", "f": ["Finger-prick sample", "Often re-tested every 6–12 months", "None", "Report usually within several weeks"], "g": ["Healthy ageing goals", "Tracking change over time", "Longevity planning"], "h": [["Discuss", "Your clinician explains what the test can and cannot tell you.", "15 min"], ["Sample", "A small finger-prick blood sample, collected in clinic or at home.", "10 min"], ["Review", "Your report is reviewed alongside your history, bloodwork and fitness.", "30–45 min"]], "q": [["Is this a genetic test?", "Not in the usual sense. It looks at methylation, chemical tags on DNA that change over time, rather than the DNA code you inherited."], ["Is it a diagnostic test?", "No. It gives estimates that can help guide and track a plan. It does not diagnose disease."], ["What are the possible side effects?", "The finger prick can cause brief discomfort and, occasionally, minor bruising at the site. There are no other side effects from the test itself."]], "caution": ["Pregnancy, which your clinician will review", "A recent acute illness, which may be worth waiting out before testing"]},"glycanage":{"n": "GlycanAge Test", "c": "longevity-testing", "s": "A finger-prick test that estimates biological age from glycans linked to inflammation.", "i": "GlycanAge estimates your biological age from glycans, sugar molecules attached to your IgG antibodies. Glycan patterns are linked to long-term, low-grade inflammation, often called inflammaging. At Mediworks in South Surrey, results are reviewed with your clinician.", "f": ["Finger-prick sample", "Can be repeated to track change", "None", "Report usually within several weeks"], "g": ["Healthy ageing goals", "Concern about chronic inflammation", "Tracking lifestyle changes"], "h": [["Discuss", "Your clinician explains what the test measures and its limits.", "15 min"], ["Sample", "A small finger-prick blood sample, collected in clinic or at home.", "10 min"], ["Review", "Your result is reviewed alongside your history and other markers.", "30 min"]], "q": [["Is this a food sensitivity test?", "No. It looks at sugar molecules on IgG antibodies as a marker of inflammation and ageing. It is not a food sensitivity or allergy test."], ["Is it a diagnostic test?", "No. It gives an estimate that can help guide and track a plan. It does not diagnose disease."], ["What are the possible side effects?", "The finger prick can cause brief discomfort and, occasionally, minor bruising at the site. There are no other side effects from the test itself."]], "caution": ["A recent acute illness or infection, which may temporarily affect results", "Pregnancy, which your clinician will review"]},"grip-strength":{"n": "Grip Strength", "c": "longevity-testing", "s": "Checked with your routine vitals at a longevity consultation.", "i": "Grip strength is a quick measure of how hard you can squeeze a handheld dynamometer. It reflects overall muscle strength and, in large studies, is linked to heart health and longevity. At Mediworks in South Surrey, it is not booked on its own: it is checked as part of your routine vitals during a longevity consultation, then compared with age- and sex-based norms and re-checked over time.", "f": ["A few minutes, with your vitals", "Re-checked at follow-up visits", "None", "Results the same visit"], "g": ["Healthy ageing goals", "Building or keeping muscle", "Tracking change over time"], "h": [["Vitals", "Alongside blood pressure, heart rate and weight, your clinician explains the grip test and you try a practice squeeze.", "2 min"], ["Test", "Seated with your elbow bent, you squeeze the dynamometer a few times with each hand.", "3 min"], ["Review", "Your best result is compared with age- and sex-based norms and recorded as a baseline for future visits.", "Same visit"]], "q": [["Can I book a grip strength test on its own?", "No. It is part of the routine vitals taken during a longevity consultation, so it is reviewed alongside your other results."], ["Does it hurt?", "No. You squeeze a handle as hard as you comfortably can for a few seconds."], ["Can I improve my grip strength?", "Grip strength usually responds to regular strength training. Your clinician can suggest how to build it into your plan."], ["Is it a diagnostic test?", "No. It is a simple measure of strength, tracked over time alongside your other results."]], "caution": ["A recent hand, wrist or elbow injury or surgery, in which case the test is skipped", "A painful arthritis flare in the hands"]},"genomics":{"n": "totalPower DNA Test", "c": "genetics", "s": "A one-time dnaPower test of 250+ gene variants for diet, fitness, methylation, detox, hormones and brain health, including APOE with your consent.", "i": "totalPower, from dnaPower, looks at more than 250 gene variants linked to diet, weight, vitamins, fitness and recovery, methylation (including MTHFR), detoxification, estrogen metabolism and brain health, including APOE. At Mediworks in South Surrey, it is the genetics test in the Longevity Protocol, and results are interpreted alongside your history and bloodwork.", "f": ["Cheek swab", "Usually once", "None", "Report usually within weeks"], "g": ["Personalising nutrition", "Understanding family health history", "Prevention planning"], "h": [["Discuss", "Your clinician explains what the test can and cannot tell you.", "15 min"], ["Sample", "A cheek swab or saliva sample.", "5 min"], ["Review", "Results are interpreted alongside your history and bloodwork.", "30–45 min"]], "q": [["Is this a diagnostic test?", "No. It looks at genetic tendencies rather than diagnosing disease. Results are one piece of information alongside your history and other tests."], ["Does it include APOE?", "Yes, with your full APOE type (for example e3/e3). APOE is linked to Alzheimer's and heart risk, and the test also looks at genes linked to Parkinson's. Because these results can be significant, you choose whether to receive them, and they are explained at a results visit, not by email."], ["Can my results be turned into a supplement?", "Yes. With DNA-personalized supplements, your results are used to make a supplement formula for you, reviewed by your ND. <a class=\"link\" href=\"#t-dna-supplements\">Learn about DNA-personalized supplements →</a>"], ["Is there an option that uses AI?", "Yes. SelfDecode analyses your DNA alongside your lab results with an AI health GPT, and your ND reviews every recommendation. <a class=\"link\" href=\"#t-selfdecode\">Learn about SelfDecode →</a>"], ["How is my data handled?", "Ask your clinician which laboratory is used and how samples and data are stored and protected."], ["Do I need to repeat it?", "Your genes do not change, so the test is usually done once."]], "caution": ["Concerns about inherited disease risk, which may need referral to a genetic counsellor"]},
    "mitochondria-rehab":{"n": "Mitochondria Rehab", "c": "iv-cellular", "s": "A Naturopathic protocol focused on cellular energy and recovery.", "i": "Mitochondria Rehab is a Naturopathic protocol at Mediworks in South Surrey that focuses on mitochondria, the energy-producing parts of cells. It combines nutrients, IV support, oxygen and light therapies with changes to sleep, movement and nutrition.", "f": ["Protocol", "Usually several weeks", "None", "Reviewed over weeks"], "g": ["Fatigue and low stamina", "Slow recovery from exercise or illness", "Healthy ageing goals"], "h": [["Assess", "A review of symptoms, history and relevant bloodwork.", "60 min"], ["Plan", "A combination of therapies and lifestyle steps chosen for you.", "Visit 2"], ["Follow", "Scheduled sessions over several weeks.", "As planned"], ["Review", "Progress is reviewed and the plan adjusted.", "End of protocol"]], "q": [["Which therapies are included?", "Plans can include nutrients, IV therapies, LiveO2, Red Light Therapy and guidance on sleep, movement and nutrition. Your clinician selects what suits you."], ["Is fatigue investigated first?", "Yes. Ongoing fatigue can have many causes, so an assessment and appropriate bloodwork come first."], ["How long is the protocol?", "Usually several weeks. Your clinician will outline the schedule."]], "caution": ["Fatigue that has not been medically assessed", "Pregnancy or breastfeeding", "Heart, lung or kidney conditions, which your clinician will review"]},
    "liveo2":{"n": "LiveO2 Adaptive Contrast", "c": "recovery-performance", "s": "Exercise while switching between oxygen-rich and reduced-oxygen air.", "i": "LiveO2 Adaptive Contrast is an exercise-with-oxygen system. At Mediworks in South Surrey, you ride a stationary bike while switching between oxygen-rich and reduced-oxygen air, with oxygen levels and heart rate monitored. It may be used for brain fog, concussion recovery support, energy and exercise recovery.", "f": ["About 15–25 min", "Often a series", "None", "Reviewed over several sessions"], "g": ["Brain fog and focus", "Supportive care after a concussion", "Energy and endurance", "Exercise recovery"], "h": [["Screen", "A health review to confirm LiveO2 is suitable.", "15 min"], ["Set up", "You are fitted with a mask and monitors.", "5 min"], ["Session", "Cycling at your own level while switching air supply.", "15–25 min"]], "q": [["Do I need to be fit?", "No. The exercise level is set for you and can be adjusted during the session."], ["Can it help with brain fog or after a concussion?", "LiveO2 may be included as supportive care for brain fog or after a concussion, alongside your physician's care. Your clinician confirms it is safe for you to exercise first."], ["Is it the same as hyperbaric oxygen?", "No. LiveO2 is done during exercise at normal pressure. Mediworks offers LiveO2, not hyperbaric oxygen therapy."], ["What does the evidence say?", "Research on oxygen contrast training is limited. Your clinician will explain what is known and whether it suits your goals."], ["Who should not use it?", "People with certain heart or lung conditions may not be suitable. Your clinician reviews your health first."]], "caution": ["Unstable heart conditions, chest pain or recent heart events", "Severe lung disease", "Uncontrolled high blood pressure", "Pregnancy", "Seizure disorders, which your clinician will review"]},
    "red-light-therapy":{"n": "ARRC Red Light", "c": "recovery-performance", "s": "Full-body red and near-infrared light on the ARRC LED bed, for cellular energy, recovery, focus, sleep and skin.", "i": "Red Light Therapy, also called photobiomodulation, uses red and near-infrared light. At Mediworks in South Surrey, ARRC red light sessions of about 10 to 20 minutes are offered to support cellular energy, recovery, joint and muscle comfort, focus, relaxation and sleep, skin quality and healthy ageing.", "f": ["About 10–20 min", "Often 2–3 times a week to start", "None", "Gradual, over weeks"], "g": ["Low energy and fatigue", "Exercise recovery", "Joint and muscle comfort", "Focus and mental clarity", "Relaxation and sleep", "Skin tone and texture"], "h": [["Prepare", "Remove makeup if the face is being treated. Eye protection is provided.", "5 min"], ["Session", "Relax on the full-body ARRC bed while the light runs.", "10–20 min"]], "q": [["Does it hurt?", "No. Most people feel gentle warmth."], ["How often should I come?", "Regular sessions are usually recommended. Your clinician will suggest a schedule."], ["Is it safe for the eyes?", "Eye protection is provided. Tell us if you take medications that increase sensitivity to light."]], "caution": ["Medications or conditions that increase light sensitivity", "Pregnancy, which your clinician will review", "A history of skin cancer in the treatment area", "Epilepsy triggered by light"]},
    "vasper":{"n": "Vasper", "c": "recovery-performance", "soon": true, "s": "Cooling, compression and low-impact exercise. Coming soon.", "i": "Vasper is a short, low-impact workout that combines cooling and compression with interval exercise. Mediworks in South Surrey is planning to add Vasper to the clinic.", "f": ["About 20 min", "A series", "None", "Varies"], "g": ["Time-efficient exercise", "Recovery", "Low-impact training"], "q": [["When will it be available?", "A launch date has not been confirmed. Contact the clinic to register your interest."]]},
    "aesthetic-consultation":{"n": "Naturopathic Aesthetic Consultation", "c": "injectables", "s": "The first step for aesthetic treatment: an assessment and a plan.", "i": "A Naturopathic Aesthetic Consultation is a visit with a Naturopathic Doctor at Mediworks in South Surrey to assess your skin, face and goals and explain your options. It is the first step for new aesthetic patients.", "f": ["Consultation", "One visit", "None", "A plan at the visit"], "g": ["Not sure which treatment suits you", "Comparing options for lines, volume or skin quality", "Under-eye concerns (required before Under-Eye Filler)", "Planning skin care over time"], "h": [["Before", "Complete your intake forms.", "Before your visit"], ["Assess", "Your skin, face, health history and goals are reviewed.", "Consultation"], ["Plan", "Your options are explained, including risks, costs and alternatives.", "Same visit"], ["Book", "If you choose a treatment, it is booked when you are ready.", "When you are ready"]], "q": [["Is any treatment done at this visit?", "For some treatments, such as a first Neuromodulator, filler, PRP Facial or Microneedling, treatment may be done the same day after the consultation if it is suitable. Under-Eye Filler and hair treatments are always booked for a separate visit."], ["Do I need this before Under-Eye Filler?", "Yes. Every new Under-Eye Filler patient has this consultation first. The area is assessed carefully and other options are discussed. If filler is suitable, it is booked for a separate visit."], ["What should I bring?", "A list of your medications and supplements, and details of any previous aesthetic treatments."], ["Is it covered by insurance?", "Naturopathic consultations may be covered by extended health plans, and we offer direct billing. Please check your plan."]]},
    "hair-consultation":{"n": "Naturopathic Hair Consultation", "c": "hair", "s": "The first step before any hair treatment.", "i": "A Naturopathic Hair Consultation is a visit with a Naturopathic Doctor at Mediworks in South Surrey to review your history, scalp, medications and bloodwork. It looks for possible contributing factors before any hair treatment is recommended.", "f": ["Consultation", "One visit, then treatment visits if planned", "None", "A plan at the visit"], "g": ["Thinning or shedding hair", "Considering PRP or PRF for hair", "Hair Loss after illness, stress or pregnancy", "Wanting to understand possible causes"], "h": [["Before", "Complete your intake forms and bring any recent lab results.", "Before your visit"], ["Assess", "Scalp, history, medications and any bloodwork needed.", "Consultation"], ["Plan", "Whether treatment is suitable, and which options to consider.", "Same visit"], ["Book", "Treatments are scheduled for a later visit.", "Next visit"]], "q": [["Can I have hair PRP on the same day?", "No. An assessment comes first. If PRP suits you, treatment is booked for a later visit."], ["Will I need bloodwork?", "Often. Iron, thyroid and hormone levels, among others, can be relevant to Hair Loss. Your clinician will advise."], ["Is it covered by insurance?", "Naturopathic consultations may be covered by extended health plans, and we offer direct billing. Please check your plan."]]},
    "naturopathic-consultation":{"n": "Naturopathic Consultation", "c": "naturopathic", "s": "The first step for most new patients.", "i": "A Naturopathic Consultation is a 45 to 60 minute visit with a Naturopathic Doctor at Mediworks in South Surrey. It reviews your symptoms, history, medications, supplements and goals, and ends with a plan and any testing that may help.", "f": ["About 45–60 min", "Follow-ups as needed", "None", "A plan at the visit"], "g": ["Not sure where to start", "Ongoing symptoms you would like assessed", "A personalised plan", "Before hormone or Weight Loss treatment"], "h": [["Before", "Complete your intake forms and bring recent labs.", "15 min"], ["Consult", "A detailed review of your health and goals.", "45–60 min"], ["Plan", "Recommendations, testing and next steps.", "Same visit"], ["Follow up", "Review results and adjust.", "2–6 weeks"]], "q": [["Can I do it virtually?", "Yes. Many consultations and follow-ups can be done by video."], ["What should I bring?", "Recent lab results, a list of medications and supplements, and any questions you have."], ["Is it covered by insurance?", "Naturopathic consultations may be covered by extended health plans, and we offer direct billing. Please check your plan."], ["Will you work with my family doctor?", "Yes. With your consent, we can share results and coordinate care with your other healthcare providers."]]},
    "functional-lab-testing":{"n": "Functional Lab Testing", "c": "functional-labs", "s": "Specialised tests for hormones, digestion, nutrients and more, including the Organic Acids Test (OAT).", "i": "Functional lab tests are specialised tests that go beyond routine bloodwork, such as hormone metabolism, gut health and nutrient status. At Mediworks in South Surrey, your clinician recommends tests only when the results are likely to inform your plan.", "f": ["Sample collection", "As needed", "None", "Results usually in 1–4 weeks"], "g": ["Ongoing fatigue", "Digestive symptoms", "Hormone concerns", "Personalising supplements"], "q": [["What is the Organic Acids Test (OAT)?", "An at-home urine test of organic acids, the by-products of metabolism. It looks at energy production and mitochondrial function, neurotransmitter balance, detoxification, nutrient needs and gut microbial balance. It may be considered for fatigue, brain fog or headaches, mood changes, digestive symptoms, muscle weakness or pain, poor sleep, or past toxin exposure. It is a screen, not a diagnosis."], ["Are these tests covered?", "Most functional tests are paid privately. Costs are explained before anything is ordered."], ["How are they different from routine bloodwork?", "Routine tests are designed mainly to detect disease. Functional tests look at patterns such as hormone metabolism or digestion. Some have less established evidence, and your clinician will explain the strengths and limits of each."], ["Do I need to stop supplements before testing?", "Sometimes. You will receive specific instructions for each test."]], "h": [["Discuss", "Your clinician explains which tests may help and why.", "Consultation"], ["Collect", "Blood, stool, urine or saliva, depending on the test, often at home.", "As instructed"], ["Review", "Results are reviewed with you and your plan is updated.", "Follow-up"]]},
    "lifelabs-testing":{"n": "Conventional Labs (LifeLabs)", "c": "bloodwork", "s": "LifeLabs panels for hormones, thyroid, metabolism and Insulin Resistance (HOMA-IR), iron, autoimmune markers and more.", "i": "Conventional lab tests, such as hormone and thyroid panels, iron, vitamin D, blood sugar, Insulin Resistance (HOMA-IR) and cholesterol, are ordered through LifeLabs by your clinician at Mediworks in South Surrey. Results are reviewed with you in plain language.", "f": ["A quick blood draw", "As needed", "None", "Results usually in days"], "g": ["A baseline health check", "Monitoring a treatment", "Investigating symptoms"], "h": [["Order", "Your clinician selects tests based on your symptoms and goals.", "Consultation"], ["Draw", "Visit any LifeLabs location with your requisition.", "10–15 min"], ["Review", "Results are explained at your follow-up.", "Follow-up"]], "q": [["Are LifeLabs tests covered?", "Mediworks is private pay, so LifeLabs tests ordered by our clinicians are paid privately. Some extended health plans reimburse lab fees. Your clinician explains costs before ordering."], ["Do I need to fast?", "Some tests, such as fasting glucose, insulin and some cholesterol panels, need fasting. Your requisition will say."], ["Can I share results with my family doctor?", "Yes. With your consent, we can share results."]]},
    "holistic-nutrition":{"n": "Holistic Nutrition", "c": "naturopathic", "s": "Practical eating plans with a Registered Holistic Nutritionist.", "i": "Holistic Nutrition looks at how food, digestion and lifestyle relate to energy, weight, mood and skin. At Mediworks in South Surrey, Joyce Hoffmann, RHN, builds realistic eating plans around your goals, preferences and schedule.", "f": ["About 60 min", "Follow-ups as needed", "None", "Reviewed at follow-ups"], "g": ["Digestive issues", "Weight and energy", "Food sensitivities", "Meal planning"], "h": [["Before", "Complete an intake form and, if possible, a short food diary.", "Before your visit"], ["Review", "Your current eating, digestion and lifestyle are discussed.", "40 min"], ["Plan", "Practical meal ideas and habits to start with.", "20 min"], ["Follow up", "The plan is adjusted as you go.", "As needed"]], "q": [["What is an RHN?", "A Registered Holistic Nutritionist is trained in whole-food nutrition. An RHN does not diagnose or treat medical conditions; your Naturopathic Doctor or physician does that."], ["Will I get a meal plan?", "You will get practical meal ideas and habits that fit your schedule and preferences."], ["Is it covered by insurance?", "Some extended health plans cover Holistic Nutrition. Please check your plan."]]},
    "supplement-protocols":{"n": "Supplements", "c": "naturopathic", "s": "Professional-grade supplements, recommended based on your history and testing.", "i": "Supplement protocols are personalised recommendations from a Naturopathic Doctor at Mediworks in South Surrey. They are based on your history and testing, checked against your medications and reviewed over time.", "f": ["Part of your visit", "Reviewed regularly", "None", "Weeks"], "g": ["Nutrient deficiencies", "Supporting a treatment plan", "Simplifying what you take"], "q": [["Can I order online?", "Yes. Recommended products can be ordered through our online dispensary."], ["Do you check for interactions?", "Yes. Your clinician reviews supplements against your medications and health conditions."], ["Should I stop my current supplements?", "Bring a list of everything you take. Your clinician will advise what to continue, change or stop."], ["Can my supplements be based on my DNA?", "Yes. DNA-personalized supplements use a cheek-swab genetic test to make a formula for you, which your ND reviews alongside your bloodwork. <a class=\"link\" href=\"#t-dna-supplements\">Learn more →</a>"]]},
    "slit":{"n": "Sublingual Immunotherapy", "c": "naturopathic", "s": "Allergy drops taken under the tongue at home.", "i": "Sublingual Immunotherapy (SLIT) uses small, gradually increasing doses of an allergen taken as drops under the tongue. At Mediworks in South Surrey, triggers are confirmed with testing first, then drops prepared by Western Allergy Group are taken daily at home with regular review.", "f": ["Consultation + testing", "Daily drops, often for 3–5 years", "None", "Often assessed over months"], "g": ["Seasonal allergies", "Dust mite or pet allergies", "An alternative to allergy shots"], "q": [["Do I need allergy testing first?", "Yes. Your triggers are confirmed before starting."], ["Who prepares the drops?", "Drops are prepared by Western Allergy Group based on your confirmed allergy triggers."], ["How long does treatment take?", "Daily use for three to five years is common. Your clinician will review progress regularly."], ["What are the possible side effects?", "Itching or tingling in the mouth is common at first. Serious allergic reactions are rare; your clinician will explain what to watch for."], ["Can I stop my allergy medication?", "Do not stop medication without talking to your clinician."], ["Is it covered by insurance?", "SLIT may be covered by some extended health plans. Please check your plan."]], "h": [["Assess", "A review of your symptoms and history.", "30 min"], ["Test", "Allergy testing to confirm your triggers.", "As needed"], ["Start", "Your first dose is often given in clinic so you can be observed.", "30 min"], ["Continue", "Daily drops at home, with regular review.", "Ongoing"]], "caution": ["Severe or uncontrolled asthma", "A history of severe allergic reactions (anaphylaxis)", "Mouth sores or recent dental surgery", "Pregnancy, which your clinician will review"]},
    "myers-cocktail":{"n": "IV Nutrient Therapy", "c": "iv-cellular", "s": "Vitamins, minerals and other nutrients given by IV, after a health screen.", "i": "IV Therapy, often called an IV drip, delivers vitamins, minerals and other nutrients directly into the bloodstream. At the Mediworks Drip Lounge in South Surrey, each IV is formulated after a health screen, with options including the Myers' Cocktail, glutathione, IV iron, procaine and vitamin B12 shots.", "f": ["About 30–60 min", "As advised", "None", "Varies"], "g": ["Low energy", "Recovery after travel or illness", "Low iron when tablets are not enough", "Antioxidant support"], "q": [["Is it safe?", "Every IV is formulated after a health screen and given by trained staff. Tell us about your medications and health conditions."], ["Which IV is right for me?", "Your Naturopathic Doctor recommends a formula after your health screen, based on your goals and any lab results."], ["What is in a Myers' Cocktail?", "It typically contains magnesium, calcium, B vitamins and vitamin C. Your clinician will confirm the formula."], ["What are the possible side effects?", "Bruising, tenderness, a warm sensation or light-headedness are possible. Rare reactions are reviewed with you first."], ["Is it covered by insurance?", "Some extended health plans cover Naturopathic services. Please check your plan."]], "h": [["Screen", "A health screen, including medications and any recent bloodwork.", "15 min"], ["Prepare", "Your clinician confirms the formula and places a small IV line.", "10 min"], ["Infuse", "You relax in the Drip Lounge during the infusion.", "30–45 min"]], "x": [["Same day", "Mild bruising or tenderness at the IV site is possible. Most people return to normal activities."], ["Follow-up", "Your clinician discusses whether further IVs are appropriate."]], "caution": ["Pregnancy or breastfeeding", "Kidney disease or heart failure, which your clinician will review", "Allergy to any ingredient", "Some medications that may interact, which your clinician will review"]},
    "nad-iv":{"n": "NAD+ IV", "c": "iv-cellular", "s": "A slow IV infusion of NAD+, a coenzyme involved in cellular energy.", "i": "NAD+ is a coenzyme cells use to produce energy, and levels decline with age. At Mediworks in South Surrey, NAD IV Therapy is given as a slow infusion after a health screen, including as supportive care for brain fog and after a concussion.", "f": ["About 1–3 hours", "Often a series of 6–8, as advised", "None", "Varies"], "g": ["Fatigue", "Brain fog", "Supportive care after a concussion", "Healthy ageing goals"], "q": [["Why does it take so long?", "NAD+ is infused slowly for comfort. A faster rate can cause chest tightness, flushing or nausea, which usually ease when the rate is slowed."], ["Can it help with brain fog or after a concussion?", "NAD+ IV may be included as supportive care for brain fog or after a concussion, alongside your physician's care, not as a replacement for it. Research is still developing."], ["What does the evidence say?", "Research on IV NAD+ in people is still limited. Your clinician will explain what is currently known."], ["Can I work during the infusion?", "Many people read or use a laptop during the infusion."]], "h": [["Screen", "A health screen and review of medications.", "15 min"], ["Prepare", "A small IV line is placed.", "10 min"], ["Infuse", "NAD+ is infused slowly. The rate is adjusted for comfort.", "2–4 hours"]], "caution": ["Pregnancy or breastfeeding", "Kidney disease or heart failure, which your clinician will review", "Allergy to any ingredient", "Some medications that may interact, which your clinician will review"]},
    "pc-iv":{"n": "Phosphatidylcholine IV", "c": "iv-cellular", "s": "A slow IV of phosphatidylcholine, a building block of cell membranes.", "i": "Phosphatidylcholine is a building block of cell membranes, including those of brain and nerve cells. At Mediworks in South Surrey, it is given as a slow IV after a health screen, often as part of a broader plan.", "f": ["About 60–90 min", "Often a series, as advised", "None", "Varies"], "g": ["Brain fog", "Part of a broader cognitive or recovery plan"], "q": [["Is it safe?", "Your clinician reviews your health history and medications first. Mild vein irritation or a warm sensation are possible."], ["Can it be combined with other IVs?", "Yes. It is often followed by glutathione or used alongside NAD+ as part of a plan."], ["What does the evidence say?", "Research on IV phosphatidylcholine is limited. Your clinician will explain what is known and why it may be considered for you."], ["Can it help after a concussion?", "It may be considered as supportive care alongside your physician's care, not as a replacement for it."]], "h": [["Screen", "A health screen and review of medications.", "15 min"], ["Prepare", "A small IV line is placed.", "10 min"], ["Infuse", "Phosphatidylcholine is infused slowly.", "60–90 min"]], "caution": ["Pregnancy or breastfeeding", "Kidney disease or heart failure, which your clinician will review", "Allergy to any ingredient", "Some medications that may interact, which your clinician will review", "Allergy to soy, as some products are soy-derived"]},
    "glutathione-iv":{"n": "Glutathione IV", "c": "iv-cellular", "s": "A short IV push of glutathione, often added to another IV.", "i": "Glutathione is an antioxidant made by the body's cells. At Mediworks in South Surrey, it is usually given as a short IV push, often at the end of another infusion, after a health screen.", "f": ["About 10–20 min", "On its own or added to another IV", "None", "Varies"], "g": ["Antioxidant support", "An add-on to another IV"], "q": [["Why is it added to another IV?", "It is often given at the end of another infusion, such as phosphatidylcholine, so only one visit is needed."], ["Will it lighten my skin?", "Glutathione is sometimes promoted for skin lightening. Mediworks does not offer it for that purpose, and evidence for this use is limited."], ["What are the possible side effects?", "Bruising or tenderness at the IV site. Allergic reactions are rare."]], "caution": ["Pregnancy or breastfeeding", "Asthma, as glutathione may rarely trigger symptoms", "Allergy to any ingredient"]},
    "prp-facial":{"caution": ["Platelet disorders, or blood thinners that raise bleeding risk", "An infection at the treatment site, or feeling unwell on the day", "Active cancer or current cancer treatment", "Some autoimmune or inflammatory conditions, which your clinician will review", "Pregnancy or breastfeeding"], "n": "PRP Facial", "c": "regenerative-skin", "s": "Platelet-Rich Plasma from your own blood, applied to the skin.", "i": "A PRP Facial uses Platelet-Rich Plasma prepared from a small sample of your own blood. It is applied with Microneedling or placed with fine injections, usually as a series of three sessions in South Surrey.", "f": ["About 60–75 min", "Usually 3 sessions, 4–6 weeks apart", "Usually 1–2 days", "Gradual, over several weeks"], "g": ["Fine lines and uneven texture", "Hyperpigmentation or rosacea", "Scars and enlarged pores", "Preferring your own natural material"], "h": [["Blood draw", "A small sample, similar to a routine lab test.", "5 min"], ["Prepare", "A centrifuge separates the Platelet-Rich Plasma in a sterile, single-use kit.", "15 min"], ["Numb", "Numbing cream is applied.", "20 min"], ["Treat", "PRP is applied with Microneedling or fine injections.", "20 min"]], "q": [["Is PRP the same as a \"vampire facial\"?", "The term is often used for PRP applied with Microneedling. At Mediworks it is described as a PRP Facial."], ["Who performs the treatment?", "Injectable treatments at Mediworks are performed only by our Naturopathic Doctors, after a consultation."], ["PRP or PRF?", "Both use your own platelets. PRF is spun more gently, without additives, and releases growth factors more slowly. Your clinician will recommend one for your skin."], ["Is it safe?", "Because PRP is made from your own blood, the risk of allergic reaction is low. Bruising, redness, swelling and tenderness are common. Infection is rare."], ["How many sessions will I need?", "Most plans include three sessions about four to six weeks apart, followed by maintenance if you choose."]], "tags": "dull texture under", "x": [["Days 1–2", "Redness, mild swelling and tenderness are common."], ["Days 3–5", "Skin may feel dry. Use gentle skincare and sunscreen."], ["Weeks 4–6", "The next session is booked if planned."], ["Months 2–3", "Collagen remodelling continues gradually."]]},
    "prf-facial":{"n": "PRF", "c": "regenerative-skin", "s": "An additive-free platelet treatment, often used for the under-eyes.", "i": "PRF (Platelet-Rich Fibrin) is prepared from your own blood using a slower spin and no additives. It is placed with fine injections or Microneedling, and is often used for the under-eye area and skin texture in South Surrey.", "f": ["About 60 min", "Usually 3 sessions, 4–6 weeks apart", "Usually 1–2 days", "Gradual, over several weeks"], "g": ["Tired or hollow under-eyes", "Fine lines and crepey skin", "Preferring an additive-free option"], "h": [["Blood draw", "A small sample is taken from your arm.", "5 min"], ["Spin", "A slower spin keeps the fibrin intact.", "10 min"], ["Numb", "Numbing cream is applied.", "20 min"], ["Treat", "PRF is placed with fine injections or Microneedling.", "20 min"]], "q": [["PRF or PRP?", "Both use your own platelets. PRF is spun more slowly without anticoagulants, so growth factors are released over a longer period. Your clinician will recommend one for your skin."], ["Who performs the treatment?", "Injectable treatments at Mediworks are performed only by our Naturopathic Doctors, after a consultation."], ["Why is it used under the eyes?", "PRF can be placed in small amounts in thin skin, such as under the eyes. Your clinician will assess the area first."], ["What are the possible side effects?", "Swelling, redness, tenderness and bruising are common, particularly under the eyes, and usually settle within days."]], "tags": "under texture dull", "x": [["Days 1–2", "Mild swelling, redness and possible bruising, especially under the eyes."], ["Weeks 4–6", "The next session is booked if planned."], ["Months 2–3", "Collagen remodelling continues gradually."]], "caution": ["Platelet disorders, or blood thinners that raise bleeding risk", "An infection at the treatment site, or feeling unwell on the day", "Active cancer or current cancer treatment", "Some autoimmune or inflammatory conditions, which your clinician will review", "Pregnancy or breastfeeding"]},
    "prfm":{"n": "PRFM", "c": "regenerative-skin", "s": "A gel prepared from your own platelets, placed as a soft filler.", "i": "PRFM (Platelet-Rich Fibrin matrix) is a denser, gel-like preparation of your own platelets. It is placed like a soft filler for under-eyes, fine lines and shallow scars, offered in South Surrey after a consultation.", "f": ["About 60 min", "Usually 1–3 sessions", "Usually 1–3 days", "Gradual, over about 1–3 months"], "g": ["Under-eye hollows", "Fine lines and shallow scars", "Wanting a natural alternative to filler"], "h": [["Blood draw", "A small sample is taken from your arm.", "5 min"], ["Prepare", "Your platelets are concentrated into a soft matrix.", "15 min"], ["Numb", "Numbing is applied.", "15 min"], ["Treat", "PRFM is placed with a fine needle or cannula.", "20 min"]], "q": [["How is PRFM different from filler?", "It uses only your own blood, so the change is generally subtler than with hyaluronic acid filler and develops as the matrix settles."], ["Who performs the treatment?", "Injectable treatments at Mediworks are performed only by our Naturopathic Doctors, after a consultation."], ["How long does it last?", "It varies between people. Your clinician will discuss what to expect and when to review."], ["What are the possible side effects?", "Swelling, tenderness and bruising at the injection and blood draw sites are common and usually short-lived."]], "tags": "under volume", "x": [["Same day", "Soft fullness and some swelling are common."], ["Days 1–3", "Swelling and any bruising usually settle."], ["Weeks 4–12", "Your clinician reviews the area and discusses whether another session is needed."]], "caution": ["Platelet disorders, or blood thinners that raise bleeding risk", "An infection at the treatment site, or feeling unwell on the day", "Active cancer or current cancer treatment", "Some autoimmune or inflammatory conditions, which your clinician will review", "Pregnancy or breastfeeding"]},
    "pharmaceuticals-hair":{"n": "Pharmaceutical Hair Treatment", "c": "hair", "s": "Prescription and compounded medications for Hair Loss.", "i": "Prescription and compounded medications, used on the scalp or taken by mouth, are a common part of Hair Loss care. At Mediworks in South Surrey, options are chosen after reviewing your history and bloodwork, with regular follow-up.", "f": ["About 30 min consultation", "Usually daily, ongoing", "None", "Gradual, often assessed at 3–6 months"], "g": ["Male or female pattern thinning", "Support alongside PRP or Exosomes", "An at-home option"], "q": [["Are there side effects?", "Some medications can cause side effects. Your clinician reviews them with you before starting and monitors you over time."], ["How long before I know if it is working?", "Changes in hair are slow. Progress is usually reviewed after three to six months of consistent use."], ["Can I stop the medication?", "If treatment is stopped, any benefit is usually gradually lost. Talk to your clinician before making changes."], ["Who prescribes it?", "Prescriptions are provided by a clinician with the appropriate prescribing authority, after an assessment."]], "h": [["Assess", "Your clinician reviews your history, scalp and type of Hair Loss.", "15 min"], ["Test", "Bloodwork is arranged if needed.", "As needed"], ["Plan", "Options, side effects and monitoring are discussed.", "15 min"]], "x": [["Months 1–3", "Some people notice temporary shedding when starting certain medications."], ["Months 3–6", "Your clinician reviews progress and any side effects."], ["Ongoing", "Treatment is usually continued to maintain any benefit, with regular review."]], "caution": ["Pregnancy, planning a pregnancy or breastfeeding, as some medications must be avoided", "Liver, kidney or heart conditions, which your clinician will review", "Low blood pressure", "Other medications that may interact"]},
    "growth-hormone":{"n": "Growth Hormone Therapy", "c": "hormones", "s": "Assessment first, with treatment only when medically appropriate.", "i": "Growth Hormone is produced by the pituitary gland and plays a role in muscle, bone and Body Composition. At Mediworks in South Surrey, our Naturopathic Doctors test first and prescribe treatment only when it is medically appropriate.", "f": ["About 60 min first visit", "Ongoing, with monitoring", "None", "Reviewed over months"], "g": ["Symptoms that may suggest low Growth Hormone", "Assessment before any treatment decision"], "q": [["Is it right for everyone?", "No. Treatment is considered only after testing shows a medical need. Your clinician will explain risks, benefits and alternatives."], ["What are the possible side effects?", "Possible effects include fluid retention, joint pain and changes in blood sugar. These are reviewed before starting and monitored throughout."], ["Who prescribes it?", "Growth Hormone Therapy is prescribed by our Naturopathic Doctors, only after testing and a review of your history, with regular monitoring."]], "h": [["Assess", "A detailed review of symptoms and history.", "60 min"], ["Test", "Bloodwork, including IGF-1, and referral for further testing if needed.", "As needed"], ["Discuss", "Benefits, risks and alternatives are reviewed before any decision.", "Follow-up visit"]], "caution": ["Active cancer or a history of cancer", "Pregnancy", "Uncontrolled diabetes", "A serious acute illness"]},
        "lipotropic-injections":{"n": "Lipotropic Injections", "c": "weight-metabolic", "s": "Nutrient injections offered alongside a weight protocol.", "i": "Lipotropic injections contain nutrients such as vitamin B12, methionine, inositol and choline. At Mediworks in South Surrey, they are offered as an add-on to a structured weight protocol, not as a stand-alone treatment.", "f": ["About 10 min", "Often weekly during a protocol", "None", "Varies"], "g": ["An add-on to a weight protocol", "Low B12"], "q": [["Will these help me lose weight on their own?", "No. They are offered alongside a protocol that includes nutrition and activity. Evidence for fat loss from these injections alone is limited."], ["What is in the injection?", "Common ingredients include vitamin B12, methionine, inositol and choline. Your clinician will confirm the formula."], ["What are the possible side effects?", "Soreness, redness or bruising at the injection site. Allergic reactions are rare."]], "h": [["Review", "Your clinician confirms suitability and the formula.", "5 min"], ["Inject", "A quick intramuscular injection.", "5 min"]], "x": [["Same day", "Mild soreness at the injection site is possible."], ["During the protocol", "Injections are reviewed at regular check-ins."]], "caution": ["Allergy to cobalt or vitamin B12, or any ingredient", "Pregnancy or breastfeeding", "Leber's disease (a rare eye condition), with B12", "Kidney or liver disease, which your clinician will review"]},
    "homa-ir":{"n": "Insulin Resistance (HOMA-IR)", "c": "bloodwork", "s": "A fasting blood test that estimates Insulin Resistance.", "i": "HOMA-IR is a score calculated from fasting insulin and fasting glucose that estimates Insulin Resistance. At Mediworks in South Surrey, it is used to assess metabolic health and track change over time.", "f": ["Fasting blood draw", "Often re-tested about every 3 months", "None", "Results usually in days"], "g": ["Weight gain around the middle", "Energy crashes or sugar cravings", "A family history of diabetes", "PCOS or prediabetes"], "q": [["What is a good HOMA-IR score?", "Lower generally indicates better insulin sensitivity. Your clinician will explain your score against the lab range and your health picture."], ["Why test insulin as well as glucose?", "In early Insulin Resistance, the body makes more insulin to keep glucose normal, so glucose alone may not show the change."], ["Is the test covered?", "Tests are paid privately, and some extended health plans reimburse lab fees. Costs are explained before ordering."]], "h": [["Order", "Your clinician provides a requisition.", "Consultation"], ["Fast", "Fast overnight, usually 10–12 hours, as instructed.", "Before the test"], ["Draw", "Blood is drawn for fasting insulin and glucose.", "10 min"], ["Review", "Your score is explained alongside your other results.", "Follow-up"]]},
    "arterial-stiffness":{"n": "Arterial Stiffness Index", "c": "cardio-fitness", "s": "A non-invasive measure of arterial stiffness and central blood pressure.", "i": "Arterial stiffness testing uses the SphygmoCor® XCEL to measure blood pressure close to the heart and how quickly the pulse travels through the arteries. It is a quick, non-invasive test at our South Surrey clinic.", "f": ["About 15–20 min", "Yearly or as advised", "None", "Same-day results review"], "g": ["Heart health and prevention", "A family history of heart disease", "Tracking the effect of lifestyle changes"], "h": [["Rest", "You lie down quietly so your heart rate and blood pressure settle.", "5–10 min"], ["Central blood pressure", "A cuff on your upper arm records your pulse waveform, and the XCEL calculates the pressure in your aorta, close to your heart.", "2–3 min"], ["Pulse wave velocity", "A small pen-like sensor rests on the side of your neck while a cuff on your thigh reads the pulse in your leg. The XCEL times how fast the pulse travels between the two.", "5 min"], ["Review", "Your central blood pressure, arterial stiffness and vascular age compared with people your age, and what to work on.", "10 min"]], "q": [["Does it hurt?", "No. The cuffs inflate like a regular blood pressure check, and the neck sensor simply rests on the skin."], ["How do I prepare?", "Avoid caffeine, nicotine, alcohol and exercise for about 3 hours beforehand, and wear comfortable, loose clothing."], ["What is the SphygmoCor® XCEL?", "A clinical device that measures central blood pressure and carotid-femoral pulse wave velocity without needles. Carotid-femoral pulse wave velocity is widely recognized as the reference measure of arterial stiffness."]]},
"dna-supplements": {"n": "DNA-Personalized Supplements", "c": "genetics", "s": "A cheek-swab DNA test, then a supplement formula made for you from the results.", "i": "DNA-personalized supplements start with a simple cheek-swab test through SNiP Nutrigenomics. The lab looks at gene variants linked to how your body handles nutrients, and a supplement formula is then made for you from the results. At Mediworks in South Surrey, your Naturopathic Doctor reviews your report and your formula alongside your history and bloodwork.", "f": ["Cheek swab, done at home or in clinic", "Formula refilled monthly", "None", "Report in about 3 weeks"], "g": ["Personalised supplements", "Understanding how your genes relate to nutrition", "Simplifying a long list of separate supplements"], "h": [["Consult", "Your ND reviews your health, current supplements and goals, and explains what the test can and cannot tell you.", "30 min"], ["Swab", "A painless cheek swab, mailed to the lab in a prepaid envelope.", "5 min"], ["Review", "Your ND goes through your genetic report and the proposed formula with you, alongside your bloodwork.", "30 min"], ["Formula", "Your custom formula is made and shipped, as a powder or capsules.", "About 4–6 weeks from swab"]], "x": [["Week 0", "Consultation and cheek swab."], ["About week 3", "Your genetic report is ready and reviewed with your ND."], ["About weeks 4–6", "Your first custom formula arrives."], ["Ongoing", "Your ND reviews how you're doing and adjusts your plan, including bloodwork where useful."]], "q": [["What is SNiP Nutrigenomics?", "SNiP is a nutrigenomics company that analyses gene variants (SNPs) linked to nutrient handling and makes a supplement formula from the results. Mediworks offers it with Naturopathic Doctor oversight."], ["What does the test look at?", "Gene variants linked to areas such as methylation (including MTHFR), detoxification, antioxidant needs and heart-related nutrient handling."], ["How is the supplement made?", "Your formula is compounded for you from the nutrients your results point to, and comes as a powder or capsules. Your ND reviews it first, checking for overlaps with your current supplements and medications."], ["Is this a diagnostic test?", "No. It looks at genetic tendencies, not disease. Results are one piece of information alongside your history, symptoms and bloodwork."], ["What does the research say?", "Research on matching supplements to individual gene variants is still developing. Your ND will explain what is known, and your plan is reviewed over time rather than relying on genetics alone."], ["How is my genetic data handled?", "Ask your ND about the lab's privacy policy, how your sample and data are stored, and how to request deletion."], ["Do I need to repeat the test?", "No. Your genes don't change, so the test is done once. Your formula can be reviewed and adjusted as your needs change."], ["Can I combine this with SelfDecode?", "Yes. SelfDecode gives broader health reports and AI analysis of your DNA and labs, while this test turns your DNA into a supplement formula. <a class=\"link\" href=\"#t-selfdecode\">Learn about SelfDecode →</a>"]], "caution": ["Pregnancy or breastfeeding, which needs a separate supplement review", "Prescription medications that can interact with supplements, such as blood thinners", "Kidney or liver conditions", "Concerns about inherited disease risk, which may need referral to a genetic counsellor"], "tags": "nutrigenomics nutrigenomic snip dna genetic gene mthfr custom personalised personalized supplement supplements vitamins formula"},
"selfdecode": {"n": "SelfDecode Whole Genome", "c": "genetics", "s": "Whole genome sequencing with hereditary disease screening, including BRCA1/2, analysed with SelfDecode's AI alongside your labs.", "i": "SelfDecode Whole Genome reads your entire genome and screens for hereditary disease risk, including BRCA1/2 and other genes on the ACMG list, alongside reports analysed with an AI health GPT. Screening findings are confirmed with clinical testing and genetic counselling before any decision is made. At Mediworks in South Surrey, your Naturopathic Doctor uses SelfDecode's reports and AI analysis to inform your plan, and reviews every recommendation with you.", "f": ["At-home sample kit", "Once, with re-analysis as science advances", "None", "Reports usually within weeks"], "g": ["Understanding your genetic tendencies", "Connecting DNA with your bloodwork", "Personalised diet, sleep, exercise and supplement planning"], "h": [["Consult", "Your ND reviews your goals and explains what the test and the AI analysis can and cannot tell you.", "30 min"], ["Sample", "You complete a SelfDecode whole genome sample kit at home and mail it to the lab.", "5 min"], ["Analyse", "SelfDecode's AI GPT analyses your DNA alongside the lab results and health information your ND adds.", "A few weeks"], ["Review", "Your ND goes through the reports and recommendations with you and builds them into your plan.", "30–45 min"]], "x": [["Week 0", "Consultation and DNA kit."], ["A few weeks later", "Your genetic reports are ready."], ["Review visit", "Your ND reviews the reports and AI analysis with you, alongside your bloodwork."], ["Ongoing", "New lab results can be added over time, so the analysis and your plan stay up to date."]], "q": [["What is SelfDecode?", "SelfDecode is a precision-health platform that combines a DNA test, lab results and lifestyle information to produce personalised health reports."], ["What does \"GPT\" mean here?", "SelfDecode includes an AI health GPT, a chat-style artificial-intelligence assistant like ChatGPT, trained to analyse your DNA, labs and lifestyle together. Your ND uses it to ask questions about your data, such as which nutrients matter most for your methylation genes."], ["Does the AI make decisions about my care?", "No. The AI is a tool your ND uses to analyse your data. Every recommendation is reviewed by your Naturopathic Doctor, who considers your history, symptoms and medications before anything becomes part of your plan."], ["What does the DNA test read?", "Your whole genome. Hereditary disease findings, such as BRCA1/2, are screening results, not a diagnosis, and are confirmed with clinical testing and genetic counselling through your family doctor or BC's hereditary cancer program."], ["Should I use this if cancer runs in my family?", "If you have a strong family history of cancer, ask your family doctor about clinical genetic testing first. SelfDecode is a screening tool, not a replacement for it."], ["How accurate are the risk reports?", "Genetic risk scores are estimates, and their accuracy varies with ancestry, because most genetic research has been done in people of European descent. Your ND will put any risk report in context."], ["How is my genetic data handled?", "Your data is processed by SelfDecode. Ask your ND about SelfDecode's privacy policy, how your data is stored and how to request deletion before you test."], ["How is this different from DNA-personalized supplements?", "SelfDecode gives broad health reports and AI analysis across diet, sleep, exercise and supplements. DNA-personalized supplements turn a DNA test into a supplement formula made for you. Your ND can explain which suits your goals, or how they work together."]], "caution": ["Concerns about inherited disease risk, which may need referral to a genetic counsellor", "Anyone who would find unexpected genetic risk information distressing; your ND will talk this through first"], "tags": "selfdecode self decode dna genetic genetics gene ai gpt artificial intelligence chatgpt precision health mthfr methylation reports"}};
