  const TX_INFO={"hair-consultation": {"a": ["The Naturopathic Hair Consultation is the first step for new hair patients at Mediworks. A Naturopathic Doctor reviews your history, scalp, medications and bloodwork before any treatment is recommended."], "h": ["Hair Loss can be linked to genetics, hormones, nutrient levels, thyroid function, stress, illness and medications. Your clinician looks at these factors and examines the scalp.", "You receive a plan that may include further testing, medical options, regenerative treatments or referral."], "w": ["Thinning or shedding hair", "A widening part or receding hairline", "Hair Loss after illness, stress or pregnancy", "Patchy Hair Loss"]},"aesthetic-consultation": {"a": ["The Naturopathic Aesthetic Consultation is the first step for new aesthetic patients at Mediworks. A Naturopathic Doctor reviews your health history, assesses your skin and face, and explains which options may suit your goals."], "h": ["Your clinician reviews your medical history, medications and previous treatments, then assesses your skin and facial structure at rest and with expression.", "Options are explained with their risks, typical costs and alternatives, so you can decide in your own time."], "w": ["Choosing between aesthetic treatments", "Lines and volume changes", "Skin quality and texture", "Under-eye concerns", "Planning skin care over time"]},"pc-iv": {"a": ["Phosphatidylcholine (PC) is a phospholipid, one of the main building blocks of cell membranes, including those of brain and nerve cells. A PC IV delivers it directly into the bloodstream. Research on IV use is limited."], "h": ["Cell membranes control what moves in and out of cells and how cells signal to one another. Brain tissue is rich in phospholipids.", "Phosphatidylcholine supplies material for these membranes and for acetylcholine, a messenger involved in memory and focus. It is often combined with glutathione."], "w": ["Brain fog", "Cognitive support", "Supportive care after a concussion, alongside your physician"]}, "glutathione-iv": {"a": ["Glutathione is the body's main antioxidant and is made in every cell. A glutathione IV delivers it directly, usually as a short push at the end of another infusion."], "h": ["Glutathione neutralises free radicals and supports the liver's processing of waste products. Levels can fall with age, illness and stress.", "Given by IV, it bypasses digestion, which limits absorption from oral supplements."], "w": ["Antioxidant support", "An add-on to another IV", "Part of a recovery plan"]}, "neuromodulators": {"a": ["Neuromodulators are purified forms of botulinum toxin type A, a prescription medication. Small, measured doses are injected into specific facial muscles to temporarily reduce the movement that creates expression lines.", "Treatment at Mediworks begins with a Naturopathic Aesthetic Consultation, where your clinician reviews your health history, discusses your goals and confirms whether treatment is suitable."], "h": ["Expression lines form where muscles repeatedly contract beneath the skin. Nerves signal these muscles using a chemical messenger called acetylcholine.", "Botulinum toxin temporarily blocks that signal in the treated muscle, which reduces its movement. Nearby muscles continue to work normally. Over several months, nerve signalling gradually returns, along with muscle movement."], "w": ["Frown lines between the brows", "Horizontal forehead lines", "Crow's feet at the outer eyes", "Neck bands (platysmal bands)", "Jawline contouring (Nefertiti lift)", "Other areas, discussed individually at your assessment"]}, "therapeutic-botox": {"a": ["Therapeutic Neuromodulator treatment uses botulinum toxin type A, a prescription medication, to treat medical conditions rather than expression lines. At Mediworks it is considered for chronic migraine and excessive sweating, after a consultation confirms it is appropriate.", "Treatment is usually repeated every three to six months, depending on the condition and your response."], "h": ["For chronic migraine, small doses are injected at set points across the forehead, temples, back of the head, neck and shoulders. Botulinum toxin reduces the release of certain chemical messengers from nerve endings that are involved in pain signalling.", "For excessive sweating, it blocks acetylcholine, the messenger that activates sweat glands in the treated skin. Other areas of the body continue to sweat normally to regulate temperature."], "w": ["Chronic migraine", "Excessive underarm sweating", "Excessive sweating of the hands", "Excessive sweating of the feet"]}, "dermal-fillers": {"a": ["Dermal Fillers are gels made from hyaluronic acid (HA), a substance found naturally in the skin that binds water. They are injected to add volume or support to specific areas of the face.", "Treatment at Mediworks begins with a Naturopathic Aesthetic Consultation to review your health history, assess your facial structure and agree on a plan."], "h": ["With age, the face gradually loses bone, fat, collagen and natural hyaluronic acid, which can change its shape and support.", "HA filler is placed under the skin or along the bone to add volume where it is needed. The gel holds its shape and attracts water. Over months, the body gradually breaks it down. If needed, it can be dissolved with an enzyme."], "w": ["Cheek volume", "Under-eye hollows (tear troughs)", "Temple hollowing", "Chin and jawline definition", "Lip volume and shape", "Nose-to-mouth lines (nasolabial folds)", "Lines from the mouth to chin (marionette lines)"]}, "sculptra": {"a": ["Sculptra is an injectable made of poly-L-lactic acid (PLLA), a biocompatible material used in medicine for many years. Rather than filling an area immediately, it stimulates the skin to produce new collagen over several months.", "Treatment is usually given as a short series, after a Naturopathic Aesthetic Consultation."], "h": ["PLLA microparticles are suspended in water and injected into the deeper skin. The water is absorbed within days.", "The remaining particles stimulate fibroblasts, the cells that make collagen. Over the following months, new collagen forms around the particles, which gradually adds volume. The particles slowly break down and are absorbed by the body."], "w": ["Gradual facial volume loss", "Temple and cheek hollowing", "Mild skin laxity", "Facial thinning after Weight Loss", "Crepey skin on the neck and décolletage"]}, "biofiller": {"a": ["A Biofiller is a gel made from your own blood plasma. It is injected to add gentle volume and contains no synthetic filler material.", "It may be considered for people who prefer an option based on their own blood, or who have had reactions to synthetic fillers."], "h": ["A small blood sample is spun in a centrifuge to separate the plasma. The plasma is then heated in a controlled way so its proteins thicken into a soft, injectable gel.", "The gel is placed under the skin to add soft volume and is gradually absorbed by the body over time."], "w": ["Under-eye hollows", "Mild cheek and temple volume loss", "Fine lines around the eyes and mouth"]}, "skin-boosters": {"a": ["Skin Boosters are a fine, injectable hyaluronic acid placed in small amounts across the skin. They are used to improve skin hydration and texture rather than to add volume.", "A course is usually two to three sessions about a month apart, with maintenance discussed afterwards."], "h": ["Hyaluronic acid naturally attracts and holds water in the skin. Skin Boosters use a soft hyaluronic acid that spreads evenly through the upper layers of the skin.", "Placed through many small injections, it binds water in the skin. The process may also stimulate the cells that produce collagen and elastin."], "w": ["Dehydrated or dull skin", "Fine lines and crepey texture", "Neck and décolletage lines", "The backs of the hands"]}, "microneedling": {"a": ["Microneedling, also called collagen induction therapy, uses a medical pen with fine sterile needles to create controlled micro-channels in the skin. It is used for texture, pores and scarring, and for hyperpigmentation.", "A series of three to four sessions about a month apart is typical, planned after an assessment of your skin."], "h": ["The needles create many tiny, controlled injuries at a set depth. The skin responds with its normal healing process: inflammation, new tissue formation and remodelling.", "During healing, fibroblasts produce new collagen and elastin. For a few hours after treatment, the open channels also allow serums, PRP or Exosomes to reach deeper layers of the skin. For hyperpigmentation, your clinician may pair Microneedling with tranexamic acid, glutathione, PRP or Exosomes, depending on your skin."], "w": ["Acne scars", "Enlarged pores", "Rough or uneven texture", "Fine lines", "Neck and décolletage", "Hyperpigmentation, sun spots, melasma and post-inflammatory hyperpigmentation (PIH)", "Stretch marks", "Surgical scars"]}, "exosome-facial": {"a": ["Exosomes are tiny vesicles that cells release to communicate. In aesthetic care, Purasomes Exosomes by Avari, which are derived from colostrum, are applied to the skin immediately after Microneedling.", "They are offered as an add-on to Microneedling. Research on Exosomes in skin care is still emerging, and your clinician will explain what is currently known."], "h": ["Exosomes are tiny vesicles carrying growth factors, proteins and RNA, which cells use to communicate. Purasomes are purified Exosomes derived from colostrum and contain no living cells.", "Applied after Microneedling, they can pass through the temporary micro-channels. They are thought to support signalling involved in repair and inflammation, alongside the skin's response to Microneedling."], "w": ["Dull or tired-looking skin", "Uneven tone and texture", "Recovery after Microneedling", "Acne scars (with Microneedling)", "Neck and décolletage (with Microneedling)", "Fine lines"]}, "meta-cell-technology": {"a": ["Meta Cell Technology is an injected regenerative skin treatment. It is placed into the skin with fine injections and is aimed at overall skin quality rather than adding volume.", "It is usually done as a series. Your clinician will explain the product and how it is prepared at your consultation."], "h": ["Regenerative skin treatments deliver signalling factors into the skin that are intended to support the cells responsible for collagen and elastin.", "Any change develops gradually over the weeks following treatment. Your clinician will explain how this specific treatment works and how it applies to your skin."], "w": ["Uneven texture", "Dull or uneven tone", "Fine lines", "Early loss of firmness", "Crepey skin"]}, "medical-grade-skincare": {"a": ["Medical-Grade Skincare uses active ingredients, such as retinoids, vitamin C, peptides, hydroxy acids and sunscreen. Your clinician builds a simple routine for your skin type and plans it around your in-clinic treatments."], "h": ["Each ingredient has a different role. Retinoids increase cell turnover and support collagen production. Vitamin C is an antioxidant. Hydroxy acids loosen dead skin cells. Niacinamide supports the skin barrier.", "Daily broad-spectrum sunscreen helps protect against UV exposure, a major contributor to pigmentation and skin ageing. Used consistently, a routine supports skin between visits."], "w": ["Pigmentation and sun spots", "Melasma", "Acne and breakouts", "Fine lines", "Enlarged pores and texture", "Redness and sensitivity", "Dryness and a weakened skin barrier", "Skin care between treatments"]}, "prp-hair-restoration": {"a": ["PRP (Platelet-Rich Plasma) and PRF (Platelet-Rich Fibrin) are concentrates made from a small sample of your own blood and injected into thinning areas of the scalp. They are considered for early to moderate thinning in men and women.", "Treatment begins with a Hair Consultation to look at possible contributing factors. It is usually a series of sessions about a month apart, followed by maintenance."], "h": ["Your blood is spun in a centrifuge to concentrate the platelets, which contain growth factors such as PDGF, VEGF and IGF-1. PRF is spun more slowly without additives and forms a fibrin mesh that releases growth factors over several days.", "Injected into the scalp, these growth factors are thought to act on cells at the base of the follicle and support blood supply and the growth phase of the hair cycle. Response varies between people."], "w": ["Male pattern thinning", "Female pattern thinning", "A widening part", "A receding hairline", "Shedding after stress, illness or pregnancy", "Support after a hair transplant"]}, "exosome-hair-therapy": {"a": ["Exosome hair therapy applies Purasomes Exosomes by Avari, which are derived from colostrum, to the scalp to support thinning hair. No blood draw is needed. It is often combined with Microneedling or other hair treatments.", "Research on Exosomes for hair is still early, and treatment is planned after a Hair Consultation."], "h": ["Exosomes are tiny vesicles carrying growth factors, proteins and RNA, which cells use to communicate. Purasomes are purified Exosomes derived from colostrum and contain no living cells.", "Applied with Microneedling or injected into the scalp, they are thought to support signalling around the follicle related to inflammation, blood supply and the growth phase."], "w": ["Male pattern thinning", "Female pattern thinning", "Diffuse shedding", "Fine, weak hair", "An add-on to PRP, PRF or medication"]}, "alopecia-injections": {"a": ["Corticosteroid injections are a common first-line treatment for Alopecia Areata, a condition that causes round or oval patches of Hair Loss. Small amounts of medication are injected directly into the patches.", "Treatment is repeated every four to six weeks and reviewed regularly."], "h": ["In Alopecia Areata, the immune system targets hair follicles and pushes them into a resting state. The follicles are usually not destroyed, so regrowth is possible.", "A corticosteroid injected into the patch reduces the local immune reaction around the follicles. Because it acts locally, only a small amount reaches the rest of the body."], "w": ["Round, patchy Hair Loss on the scalp", "Patches in the beard", "Patches in the eyebrows", "Small, localised areas of loss"]}, "ultrasound-guided-prp": {"a": ["Ultrasound-guided PRP combines Platelet-Rich Plasma from your own blood with real-time ultrasound imaging, so the injection can be placed in the intended tissue. It is considered for tendon, ligament and joint problems.", "PRP is prepared in clinic using a closed, sterile, single-use system. Your clinician will explain how it is prepared and what to expect."], "h": ["Platelets contain growth factors involved in tissue repair. Spinning a blood sample concentrates them above normal blood levels. Injected into an injured tendon, ligament or joint, they are intended to support the body's repair process.", "Ultrasound lets your clinician see the area and follow the needle in real time. Many injuries are small or deep, so precise placement matters."], "w": ["Tennis and golfer's elbow", "Rotator cuff tendinopathy and partial tears", "Achilles tendinopathy", "Patellar tendinopathy (jumper's knee)", "Plantar fasciitis", "Knee, hip and shoulder Osteoarthritis", "Hamstring and gluteal tendon pain"]}, "knee-oa-injections": {"a": ["Hyaluronic acid knee injections, sometimes called viscosupplements, are used for Knee Osteoarthritis. They add hyaluronic acid to the joint fluid to support cushioning and lubrication.", "Some products are given as a single injection. One option also includes a corticosteroid. Your clinician will recommend a product at your assessment."], "h": ["Healthy joint fluid contains hyaluronic acid, which makes it thick and slippery. In Osteoarthritis, the fluid becomes thinner and less protective.", "Injecting hyaluronic acid into the knee supplements this fluid, which may reduce friction and help absorb shock. A product that also contains a corticosteroid acts on inflammation in the joint."], "w": ["Knee Osteoarthritis", "Pain with walking or stairs", "Morning stiffness", "Swelling and grinding in the knee"]}, "prolotherapy": {"a": ["Prolotherapy, short for proliferative therapy, is an injection treatment for chronic pain linked to weak or overstretched ligaments and tendons. A solution, usually concentrated dextrose, is injected where these tissues attach to bone.", "A series of treatments a few weeks apart is typical."], "h": ["Ligaments and tendons have a limited blood supply, so they may not fully heal after injury. A loose ligament can allow extra joint movement, which may contribute to ongoing pain.", "Concentrated dextrose causes a mild, controlled irritation at the injection site. This is intended to trigger the body's healing response, including the production of new collagen, over a series of treatments."], "w": ["Chronic low back pain", "Sacroiliac (SI) joint pain", "Neck pain", "Loose or unstable joints", "Old sprains that have been slow to heal", "Tendon pain at attachment points"]}, "prp-for-pain": {"a": ["PRP for pain uses a concentrate of your own platelets, injected into injured or degenerating muscles, tendons, ligaments and joints. Changes are usually gradual over weeks to months.", "PRP is prepared in clinic using a closed, sterile, single-use system. Your clinician will explain how it is prepared."], "h": ["Platelets release growth factors involved in tissue repair. Spinning a small blood sample concentrates them above normal blood levels.", "Injected into the injured tissue, these growth factors are intended to support repair. This is relevant for tissues with a limited blood supply, such as tendons and ligaments, which often heal slowly."], "w": ["Chronic tendon pain", "Partial tendon and ligament tears", "Muscle strains that have been slow to heal", "Osteoarthritis", "Plantar fasciitis", "Sports and overuse injuries"]}, "trigger-point-injections": {"a": ["Trigger Point Injections are used for tight, tender knots in muscle that cause local and referred pain. A small amount of local anaesthetic is injected into each knot.", "They are often combined with stretching, movement and other care."], "h": ["A trigger point is a small area of muscle fibres that stays contracted. It can irritate nearby nerves and refer pain to other areas, such as from the shoulders into the head.", "The needle and local anaesthetic are intended to interrupt this cycle, allowing the muscle to relax. Gentle stretching afterwards supports the effect."], "w": ["Neck and shoulder tension", "Tension-type headaches", "Upper and lower back muscle pain", "Myofascial pain", "Jaw muscle pain", "Hip and buttock muscle pain"]}, "glp1-support": {"a": ["GLP-1 support is a medically supervised approach for people who may be eligible for GLP-1 medication. It combines assessment, prescribing where appropriate and monitoring with nutrition, strength and Body Composition support."], "h": ["GLP-1 is a hormone released by the gut after eating. It signals fullness to the brain, slows how quickly the stomach empties and helps the pancreas release insulin when blood sugar rises.", "GLP-1 medications act on the same receptors for longer than the natural hormone. This can reduce appetite and support blood sugar control. Because Weight Loss can include muscle, protein, strength training and Body Composition scans are part of the plan."], "w": ["Weight that has not responded to diet and exercise", "Overweight or obesity with related health risks", "Insulin Resistance and prediabetes", "Type 2 diabetes (in coordination with your physician)", "PCOS-related weight concerns"]}, "slimworks": {"a": ["Slimworks is a Naturopathic Weight Management protocol. It combines a structured eating plan with regular coaching, check-ins and Body Composition tracking, with a focus on habits that can be maintained."], "h": ["Appetite, blood sugar, insulin and daily habits all influence weight. Slimworks uses a structured eating plan designed to steady blood sugar and reduce cravings.", "Regular coaching supports practical skills such as meal planning, eating out and managing plateaus. Body Composition tracking shows changes in fat and muscle, not just weight."], "w": ["Weight Management", "Weight gain around the middle", "Cravings", "Repeated cycles of Weight Loss and regain", "Prediabetes and Insulin Resistance"]}, "insulin-resistance": {"a": ["Insulin Resistance is common and is linked to weight gain around the middle, energy dips and a higher risk of type 2 diabetes. Care starts with testing, followed by a plan around nutrition, movement and sleep, and repeat testing."], "h": ["Insulin moves sugar from the blood into cells. When cells become resistant, the pancreas releases more insulin to keep blood sugar in range. High insulin levels encourage fat storage.", "Care aims to improve insulin sensitivity. Higher-protein, lower-glycaemic eating reduces sharp rises in blood sugar. Strength training builds muscle, which uses glucose. Sleep and stress management also affect blood sugar."], "w": ["Weight gain around the middle", "Energy dips after meals", "Sugar and carbohydrate cravings", "Prediabetes", "PCOS", "Fatty liver", "A family history of type 2 diabetes"]}, "guided-fasting": {"a": ["Fasting protocols are structured ways of timing meals, from daily time-restricted eating to periodic longer fasts. The approach is tailored to your health, medications and goals, with guidance throughout."], "h": ["After a meal, insulin rises and the body stores energy. Several hours after eating, insulin falls and the body begins to use more stored fat for fuel.", "Longer gaps between meals are also linked to autophagy, the process cells use to recycle damaged components. Research on fasting and metabolic health is ongoing, and protecting protein intake and muscle remains important."], "w": ["Weight Management", "Insulin Resistance", "Metabolic health", "Structure around eating"]}, "prolon": {"a": ["Prolon is a five-day Fasting Mimicking Diet: a pre-packaged, plant-based meal plan designed to mimic some effects of a multi-day fast while you still eat. It is usually repeated a few times a year, with guidance."], "h": ["The meals are low in calories, protein and sugar and higher in unsaturated fats. This is designed to keep nutrient-sensing pathways, such as mTOR and IGF-1, low, similar to fasting.", "Over the five days, the body shifts towards using fat for fuel. Research on repeated cycles and metabolic markers is ongoing."], "w": ["Metabolic health goals", "Weight Management", "Blood sugar and cholesterol markers", "Healthy ageing goals"]}, "rmr": {"a": ["A resting metabolic rate (RMR) test measures how many calories your body burns at rest, using the oxygen you breathe in and the carbon dioxide you breathe out."], "h": ["You lie quietly for 10–15 minutes while a mask or mouthpiece measures your breathing. Oxygen use is closely linked to the energy your body burns.", "The result shows your calories at rest, and whether your metabolism is faster or slower than expected for your size and age. It helps set realistic calorie and protein targets."], "w": ["Setting Weight Loss calorie targets", "Understanding a plateau", "Monitoring metabolism during GLP-1 care", "Healthy ageing baselines"]}, "autoimmune-panel": {"a": ["An autoimmune and inflammation panel is bloodwork that helps tell inflammatory or autoimmune joint pain apart from wear-and-tear pain."], "h": ["Markers such as rheumatoid factor and anti-CCP antibodies are linked to rheumatoid arthritis, and ANA can point to other autoimmune conditions. CRP and ESR show whether inflammation is active.", "Your clinician chooses the markers based on your symptoms, then reads the results together with your history and examination."], "w": ["Ruling out rheumatoid arthritis", "Screening for other autoimmune conditions", "Checking for active inflammation (CRP)", "Planning regenerative joint treatment"]}, "iron-ferritin": {"a": ["Iron and ferritin testing measures the iron in your blood and the iron your body has stored."], "h": ["Ferritin is the main marker of iron stores. A full iron panel may also include serum iron, transferrin saturation and a complete blood count.", "Low iron stores are common and are linked with hair shedding, pale skin and fatigue. Results are reviewed together with hormone testing when skin or hair is the concern."], "w": ["Hair shedding", "Skin quality", "Fatigue", "Planning aesthetic treatment"]}, "pillcheck": {"a": ["Pillcheck is a pharmacogenomic test: it reads genes that affect how your body processes medications."], "h": ["Genes such as CYP2D6 and CYP2C19 affect how quickly some medications are broken down. A faster or slower system can mean side effects or a drug that does not work as expected.", "The report groups medications by how your genes may affect them, with a pharmacist's written opinion for your prescriber."], "w": ["Several medications", "Side effects", "A medication that did not work", "Planning long-term treatment"]}, "styku-scan": {"a": ["Styku is a quick, contact-free 3D body scan. In about 30 seconds it builds a 3D model of your body, measuring shape and circumferences and estimating Body Composition."], "h": ["You stand on a slowly rotating platform while infrared depth sensors capture the surface of your body. Software builds these into a 3D model.", "From that model, Styku measures circumferences such as waist, hips, thighs and arms, and estimates body fat percentage. Comparing scans shows where your shape is changing, even when weight stays the same."], "w": ["Tracking change during Weight Loss", "Tracking muscle gain", "Monitoring during GLP-1 care", "Waist and hip measurements", "Posture overview"]}, "dexa-scan": {"a": ["A DEXA Scan measures Body Composition and bone density. It shows fat, lean muscle and bone, region by region, including visceral fat. Mediworks arranges the scan at a partner clinic and reviews the results with you."], "h": ["DEXA (dual-energy X-ray absorptiometry) passes two very low-dose X-ray beams through the body. Fat, lean tissue and bone absorb each energy differently, so the scanner can measure all three.", "The report maps where you carry fat and muscle, including visceral fat around the organs, which is linked to metabolic and heart risk. It also measures bone density."], "w": ["Body fat and lean muscle measurement", "Visceral fat", "Bone density", "Monitoring muscle during Weight Loss", "Tracking strength training", "Healthy ageing baselines"]}, "bhrt": {"a": ["Bioidentical Hormone Replacement Therapy (BHRT) uses hormones with the same molecular structure as those the body makes, such as estradiol, progesterone and Testosterone.", "It is considered for symptoms of Perimenopause and Menopause after testing and a full review, with regular follow-up."], "h": ["Estrogen, progesterone and Testosterone act on receptors throughout the body, including the brain, blood vessels, bones, skin and vaginal tissue. As levels change in Perimenopause and Menopause, symptoms such as hot flashes, poor sleep and mood changes can appear.", "Bioidentical Hormones act on these same receptors. Doses and forms are chosen for you and adjusted over time with follow-up and, where appropriate, testing."], "w": ["Hot flashes and night sweats", "Poor sleep", "Mood changes", "Brain fog", "Low libido", "Vaginal dryness", "Irregular periods in Perimenopause"]}, "trt": {"a": ["Testosterone Replacement Therapy (TRT) is a medical treatment for men with low Testosterone. The Mediworks protocol is run by Dr. Birpal Pannu, MD and Stephen Martin, NP, with virtual visits, bloodwork and regular follow-up throughout the year.", "Possible contributing factors, such as sleep, weight, stress and medications, are reviewed first. Treatment is recommended only when testing confirms it is appropriate."], "h": ["Testosterone plays a role in muscle, bone, libido, red blood cell production, energy and mood. Levels decline gradually with age and can be lower with weight gain, poor sleep, stress, illness or some medications.", "When low levels are confirmed, Testosterone Therapy, prescribed at Mediworks as an injection, aims to bring them into a normal range. Your plan is adjusted based on symptoms and bloodwork, and safety markers such as haematocrit and PSA are monitored."], "w": ["Low energy and motivation", "Low libido", "Erectile changes", "Loss of muscle and strength", "Low mood and irritability", "Poor focus"]}, "vo2-max": {"a": ["VO2 Max Testing measures the maximum amount of oxygen your body can use during exercise. Cardiorespiratory fitness is associated with long-term health, and the test also gives personal heart rate training zones."], "h": ["Muscles need oxygen to produce energy. VO2 max reflects how well the heart, lungs, blood and muscles work together to take in, deliver and use oxygen at peak effort.", "During the test, you exercise on a bike or treadmill while a mask measures the oxygen you breathe in and the carbon dioxide you breathe out. The results show your peak oxygen use and the points that define your training zones."], "w": ["Measuring cardiorespiratory fitness", "Setting heart rate training zones", "Training for endurance events", "Tracking fitness over time"]}, "truage":{"a": ["Epigenetic tests look at DNA methylation: small chemical tags on your DNA that switch genes on or off. Methylation patterns change with age and are influenced by lifestyle, so they can be used to estimate biological age."], "h": ["Researchers have built statistical models, often called epigenetic clocks, that estimate age from methylation patterns at many points on the DNA. Some estimate overall biological age, and others estimate how fast you are aging now.", "TruAge reports your estimated biological age and pace of aging. The TruHealth report adds further estimates related to health and lifestyle. Results are estimates, not diagnoses, and are most useful when compared with your own repeat tests."], "w": ["Estimating biological age", "Measuring pace of aging", "Tracking change over time", "Longevity planning"]},"glycanage":{"a": ["Glycans are sugar molecules attached to proteins. GlycanAge looks at the glycans on your IgG antibodies, a part of the immune system. Their pattern shifts with age and with long-term inflammation."], "h": ["Inflammaging is the low-grade, long-term inflammation that tends to rise with age and is linked in research to many age-related conditions. Some glycan patterns are associated with more inflammation, and others with less.", "GlycanAge turns that pattern into an estimated biological age. Because inflammation responds to sleep, activity, weight, diet and hormones, it is used to track how your body is responding to changes over time."], "w": ["Estimating biological age", "Looking at chronic inflammation (inflammaging)", "Tracking lifestyle changes", "Longevity planning"]},"grip-strength":{"a": ["A handheld dynamometer records the force of your grip in kilograms. It takes a few minutes during your vitals and can be repeated at each follow-up."], "h": ["Grip strength reflects overall muscle strength, which matters for mobility, balance and staying independent with age.", "In large population studies, lower grip strength has been associated with higher rates of heart disease and death from any cause, and with faster epigenetic ageing. These are associations: grip strength is a marker to track, alongside your other results."], "w": ["Measuring overall muscle strength", "A healthy-ageing baseline", "Tracking strength over time", "Context for Body Composition and VO2 max results"]},"genomics": {"a": ["totalPower DNA Test looks at variations in genes linked to nutrition, metabolism, detoxification, hormones, exercise and other traits. It is usually done once with a swab or saliva sample."], "h": ["Small differences in DNA, called single nucleotide polymorphisms (SNPs), can affect how certain enzymes and pathways work. For example, some variants relate to how the body processes caffeine, folate or fats.", "Results are interpreted alongside your history and bloodwork. They can help inform nutrition, supplement and exercise choices, but they do not diagnose disease."], "w": ["Personalised nutrition", "Supplement choices", "Exercise and training type", "Understanding family health history", "Prevention planning"]}, "mitochondria-rehab": {"a": ["Mitochondria Rehab is a structured Naturopathic protocol focused on mitochondrial health. It combines nutrients, IV support, oxygen and red light therapies with changes to sleep, movement and nutrition."], "h": ["Mitochondria turn food and oxygen into ATP, the energy cells use. Ageing, chronic stress, illness, poor sleep and inactivity can affect how well mitochondria work.", "The protocol combines nutrients involved in energy pathways, such as NAD+, CoQ10 and B vitamins, with oxygen and light therapies and lifestyle steps such as exercise and sleep."], "w": ["Ongoing fatigue", "Low stamina", "Slow recovery from exercise", "Recovery after illness", "Healthy ageing goals"]}, "liveo2": {"a": ["LiveO2 Adaptive Contrast is an exercise-with-oxygen system. You ride a stationary bike while switching between oxygen-rich and reduced-oxygen air. Sessions take about 15 to 25 minutes.", "It may be included in plans for brain fog, supportive care after a concussion (alongside your physician), energy, endurance and exercise recovery. Research on this approach is limited."], "h": ["Each session alternates between oxygen-rich air, reduced-oxygen air and exercise. The approach is designed to increase circulation and oxygen delivery to tissues. Your oxygen levels and heart rate are monitored throughout."], "w": ["Brain fog, focus and mental clarity", "Supportive care after a concussion, alongside your physician", "Energy and endurance", "Exercise performance", "Recovery after exercise", "Healthy ageing goals"], "steps": [["Build an oxygen surplus", "You breathe oxygen-rich air to build up a reserve of oxygen in your blood."], ["Open the blood vessels", "Reduced-oxygen air prompts blood vessels to widen, helping open smaller vessels and capillaries."], ["Increase circulation", "Exercise raises your heart rate and blood flow, pushing blood further into the tissues."], ["Deliver oxygen-rich blood", "You switch straight back to oxygen-rich air, so the now-open tissues receive oxygen-rich blood."]], "cmp": {"title": "LiveO2 vs hyperbaric oxygen (HBOT)", "intro": "Both involve breathing additional oxygen, but they work in different ways.", "cols": ["Hyperbaric oxygen (HBOT)", "LiveO2 Adaptive Contrast"], "rows": [["How it works", "Breathing oxygen in a pressurised chamber.", "Switching between high- and low-oxygen air while you exercise."], ["Session length", "60–90 minutes", "15–25 minutes"], ["What you do", "Lie or sit still in a chamber.", "Exercise on a bike, at a level that suits you."], ["Monitoring", "Monitored by the treating facility.", "Oxygen levels and heart rate tracked during every session."]], "note": "Mediworks offers LiveO2, not HBOT. Your Naturopathic Doctor will advise whether LiveO2 suits you."}}, "red-light-therapy": {"a": ["Red Light Therapy, or photobiomodulation, uses specific wavelengths of red and near-infrared light. The ARRC system delivers these wavelengths in a relaxing session of about 10 to 20 minutes."], "h": ["Red and near-infrared light penetrate the skin and are absorbed by an enzyme in the mitochondria called cytochrome c oxidase, which is involved in energy (ATP) production.", "Because every cell relies on mitochondria for energy, red light is studied well beyond the skin: for energy, circulation, muscle recovery, the brain and sleep. Research also suggests it may affect local blood flow and inflammatory signalling, and in the skin it is studied for its effect on collagen."], "w": ["Cellular energy (mitochondria and ATP)", "Circulation", "Exercise recovery", "Joint and muscle comfort", "Brain function and focus", "Relaxation and sleep", "Skin tone and texture", "Healthy ageing"]}, "vasper": {"a": ["Vasper is a low-impact exercise system that combines cooling, compression and interval training. It is designed to be easier on the joints than high-intensity exercise. Mediworks is planning to add Vasper to the clinic."], "h": ["Compression cuffs on the arms and legs and cooling pads are worn during a short, low-impact interval session.", "The approach is designed to create some of the training stimulus of harder exercise with less joint strain. Research on this approach is limited."], "w": ["Time-efficient exercise", "Low-impact training", "Exercise recovery", "Healthy ageing goals"]}, "naturopathic-consultation": {"a": ["A Naturopathic Doctor (ND) is a regulated healthcare professional in BC, trained in medical sciences as well as natural therapies. A Naturopathic Consultation looks at your overall health to identify factors that may be contributing to your symptoms."], "h": ["Symptoms can be influenced by several factors, such as nutrient levels, hormone changes, blood sugar, digestion, stress or sleep.", "Your ND takes a detailed history, examines you and, where helpful, orders lab testing. The plan may include nutrition, lifestyle changes, supplements, prescriptions where appropriate, IV Therapy and referrals, and is adjusted at follow-ups."], "w": ["Fatigue and low energy", "Digestive concerns", "Hormone and menstrual concerns", "Stress and sleep", "Weight and metabolism", "Skin conditions", "Not sure where to start"]}, "functional-lab-testing": {"a": ["Functional lab tests are specialised tests that go beyond routine bloodwork. They look at patterns such as hormone metabolism, digestion, nutrient status and stress hormones, and may be considered when you have ongoing symptoms."], "h": ["Routine labs are designed mainly to detect disease. Functional tests look at additional patterns, using blood, stool, urine or saliva depending on the question.", "Your clinician recommends tests that are likely to change your plan, and explains the evidence and limits of each before ordering."], "w": ["Ongoing fatigue", "Digestive symptoms and bloating", "Hormone concerns", "Nutrient status", "Stress hormone patterns", "Energy and mitochondrial function (Organic Acids Test)", "Personalising supplements"]}, "lifelabs-testing": {"a": ["Conventional lab testing is routine blood and urine work done through LifeLabs. It is a common starting point for care, and provides a baseline to track over time."], "h": ["Blood and urine tests reflect organ function, nutrient stores, hormone levels, blood sugar and cholesterol, compared against reference ranges.", "Your clinician orders tests based on your symptoms and goals, then explains the results with you in plain language."], "w": ["Health checks", "Fatigue", "Iron, B12 and vitamin D", "Thyroid function", "Blood sugar and cholesterol", "Monitoring a treatment"]}, "holistic-nutrition": {"a": ["Holistic Nutrition looks at how food, digestion and lifestyle relate to energy, weight, mood and skin. Working with Joyce Hoffmann, RHN, you receive a realistic plan built around your goals, preferences and schedule."], "h": ["What you eat affects blood sugar, digestion and the nutrients your body has to work with. Small, consistent changes can make a difference over time.", "Your nutritionist reviews your current eating, digestion and lifestyle, then suggests practical meal ideas, shopping lists and habits. Follow-ups adjust the plan as needed."], "w": ["Digestive issues and bloating", "Weight Management", "Low energy", "Food sensitivities", "Blood sugar balance", "Skin health", "Meal planning"]}, "supplement-protocols": {"a": ["Supplement protocols are personalised recommendations based on your history, symptoms and lab results. Your clinician checks them against your medications and reviews them over time, so you take only what is needed."], "h": ["Supplements can address nutrient gaps or support specific pathways in the body. Form, dose and timing affect how well they are absorbed.", "Your clinician uses your lab results to identify deficiencies, chooses professional-grade products and checks for interactions. Products can be ordered through our online dispensary."], "w": ["Nutrient deficiencies", "Energy and fatigue", "Supporting a treatment plan", "Bone and joint health", "Stress and sleep", "Simplifying what you take"]}, "slit": {"a": ["Sublingual Immunotherapy (SLIT) is a treatment for allergies that aims to make the immune system less reactive to specific allergens. Drops are taken under the tongue at home, usually daily, often for three to five years.", "Drops are prepared by Western Allergy Group. SLIT may be covered by some extended health plans."], "h": ["An allergy is an overreaction of the immune system to something usually harmless, such as pollen or dust mites. The immune system produces IgE antibodies, which trigger histamine release and symptoms.", "Regular small doses of the allergen under the tongue are taken up by immune cells in the mouth. Over months, this is intended to shift the immune response towards tolerance."], "w": ["Seasonal allergies and hay fever", "Dust mite allergy", "Pet allergies", "Mould allergy", "Allergic congestion", "Itchy, watery eyes"]}, "myers-cocktail": {"a": ["IV Nutrient Therapy delivers vitamins, minerals and other nutrients directly into the bloodstream in the Mediworks Drip Lounge. Options include the Myers' Cocktail, glutathione, IV iron, procaine and B12 injections, each chosen after a health screen."], "h": ["Nutrients taken by mouth are only partly absorbed through the gut, and absorption can be lower with digestive conditions, some medications and age. An IV bypasses the gut.", "The Myers' Cocktail typically combines magnesium, calcium, B vitamins and vitamin C. Glutathione is an antioxidant. IV iron is used to replenish iron stores when tablets are not tolerated or not effective."], "w": ["Low energy", "Recovery after illness or travel", "Low iron", "Muscle cramps and tension", "Antioxidant support"]}, "nad-iv": {"a": ["NAD+ IV Therapy delivers NAD+, a coenzyme cells need for energy production, directly into the bloodstream. It is given slowly for comfort. Research on IV NAD+ in people is still developing."], "h": ["NAD+ (nicotinamide adenine dinucleotide) is needed to turn food into ATP in the mitochondria. It is also used by enzymes involved in DNA repair.", "NAD+ levels decline with age. An IV infusion raises blood levels directly, although how this translates to effects in tissues is still being studied."], "w": ["Fatigue", "Brain fog", "Supportive care after a concussion, alongside your physician", "Healthy ageing goals", "Part of a mitochondrial protocol"]}, "prp-facial": {"a": ["A PRP Facial uses Platelet-Rich Plasma (PRP) from your own blood. It is applied with Microneedling or placed with fine injections to address skin texture, tone and fine lines.", "PRP is prepared in clinic using a closed, sterile, single-use system. How it is prepared affects the platelet concentration, and your clinician will explain the method used."], "h": ["Your blood is spun in a centrifuge to concentrate the platelets. Platelets contain growth factors, such as PDGF, TGF-beta and VEGF, that are involved in normal wound healing.", "Delivered into the skin, these growth factors may stimulate fibroblasts to produce collagen and elastin and support new small blood vessels. Changes develop gradually over the following weeks."], "w": ["Fine lines", "Uneven tone and texture", "Acne and other scars", "Enlarged pores", "Dull or tired-looking skin", "Tired under-eyes"]}, "prf-facial": {"a": ["PRF (Platelet-Rich Fibrin) is prepared from your own blood without anticoagulants or other additives. It releases growth factors more gradually than PRP.", "It is commonly used for the under-eye area and for skin texture, as a series of sessions."], "h": ["Blood is spun more slowly than for PRP and without anticoagulants. This allows a natural fibrin mesh to begin forming and keeps more white blood cells in the sample.", "Once placed, the fibrin acts as a scaffold that holds platelets and releases their growth factors over several days. These signals may support collagen production and skin repair."], "w": ["Tired or hollow-looking under-eyes", "Dark circles", "Fine lines and crepey skin", "Uneven texture", "Thin skin"]}, "prfm": {"a": ["PRFM (Platelet-Rich Fibrin matrix) is a denser, gel-like form of your own platelets and fibrin. It is placed like a soft filler for under-eyes, fine lines and shallow scars."], "h": ["After your blood is processed, the platelets and fibrin are concentrated into a thicker matrix. Once placed, the fibrin forms a soft gel that gives gentle volume.", "As it settles, the matrix acts as a scaffold that slowly releases growth factors, which may support collagen production in the treated area."], "w": ["Under-eye hollows", "Fine lines", "Shallow acne scars", "Mild volume loss", "Thin, crepey skin"]}, "pharmaceuticals-hair": {"a": ["Pharmaceutical hair treatments are prescription and compounded medications, applied to the scalp or taken by mouth, used to manage Hair Loss. Options are chosen after reviewing your history, type of Hair Loss and bloodwork."], "h": ["Pattern Hair Loss is linked mainly to DHT, a hormone made from Testosterone that can gradually shrink sensitive follicles. Blood supply and the length of the growth phase also play a role.", "Different medications act on different parts of this process. Some reduce the production of DHT. Others act on blood vessels and the growth phase. Compounded topicals can combine several ingredients in one formula."], "w": ["Male Pattern Hair Loss", "Female Pattern Hair Loss", "A receding hairline", "Thinning at the crown", "Support alongside PRP or Exosomes"]}, "growth-hormone": {"a": ["Growth Hormone Therapy is considered only when testing and symptoms show it is medically appropriate. If treatment is started, it is monitored with regular bloodwork and follow-up."], "h": ["Growth Hormone is released by the pituitary gland, mainly during deep sleep. It acts largely through IGF-1, a hormone made in the liver, and plays a role in muscle and bone maintenance and fat metabolism.", "Levels decline with age, and some adults have a true deficiency. Your clinician will explain the benefits, risks and alternatives before any decision."], "w": ["Assessment for adult Growth Hormone deficiency", "Low energy alongside other signs", "Changes in muscle and body fat", "Reduced bone density"]}, "hormone-testing": {"a": ["Comprehensive Hormone Testing measures hormones involved in energy, mood, sleep, weight and libido. Results are interpreted alongside your symptoms and history."], "h": ["Sex hormones such as estrogen, progesterone and Testosterone interact with thyroid and adrenal hormones such as cortisol and DHEA.", "Depending on the question, testing may use blood, saliva or dried urine. Timing matters, for example within the menstrual cycle or across the day for cortisol."], "w": ["Perimenopause and Menopause symptoms", "Low energy", "Low libido", "Mood changes", "Irregular periods", "Before or during Hormone Therapy"]}, "lipotropic-injections": {"a": ["Lipotropic injections contain nutrients involved in fat metabolism and energy, such as vitamin B12, methionine, inositol and choline. They are offered alongside a structured weight protocol and are not a stand-alone treatment."], "h": ["\"Lipotropic\" describes compounds involved in how the liver processes and moves fat. Methionine, inositol and choline play roles in this process.", "Vitamin B12 is needed for energy production and red blood cells. Given by injection, these nutrients bypass the gut. Evidence for their effect on fat loss is limited."], "w": ["Nutrient support during a weight protocol", "Low B12"]}, "homa-ir": {"a": ["HOMA-IR is a score calculated from fasting insulin and fasting glucose that estimates Insulin Resistance. It can show metabolic change before blood sugar or HbA1c rise."], "h": ["In early Insulin Resistance, the pancreas makes more insulin, so blood sugar can stay normal for years. Tests that measure only glucose may not show this stage.", "HOMA-IR combines fasting insulin and glucose into one score. A higher score suggests more insulin is needed to keep blood sugar in range."], "w": ["Weight gain around the middle", "Energy dips and cravings", "PCOS", "Prediabetes risk", "A family history of diabetes", "Tracking metabolic change"]}, "arterial-stiffness": {"a": ["Arterial stiffness testing measures how flexible your arteries are. The SphygmoCor® XCEL is a non-invasive system that measures blood pressure in the aorta (central blood pressure) and the speed of the pulse wave between the neck and leg (carotid-femoral pulse wave velocity).", "Arterial stiffness is a marker of cardiovascular health that can be tracked over time. Results are reviewed with you alongside your other health information."], "h": ["Healthy arteries are elastic. They expand with each heartbeat and recoil, smoothing blood flow. With age, high blood pressure, high blood sugar and inflammation, the artery walls stiffen.", "Stiffer arteries carry the pulse wave faster, and the wave reflects back toward the heart sooner, raising the pressure your heart works against. The XCEL captures both: a brachial cuff records your pulse waveform to calculate central blood pressure and augmentation index, and a neck sensor with a thigh cuff times the pulse to calculate pulse wave velocity.", "Your report includes central systolic pressure, central pulse pressure, augmentation index and pulse wave velocity, with your vascular age compared with people your age."], "w": ["Heart health and prevention", "A family history of heart disease", "High blood pressure", "Central blood pressure", "Diabetes and Insulin Resistance", "Tracking lifestyle changes"]},
"dna-supplements": {"a": ["DNA-personalized supplements combine a one-time genetic test with a supplement formula made for you. The test, through SNiP Nutrigenomics, uses a cheek swab and looks at gene variants linked to how your body handles certain nutrients.", "At Mediworks, the formula is not a stand-alone product. Your Naturopathic Doctor reviews your report, your current supplements and your bloodwork, so your plan reflects your whole health picture."], "h": ["Small differences in DNA, called single nucleotide polymorphisms (SNPs), can change how certain enzymes work. Some affect how the body uses folate and B vitamins (for example MTHFR), handles antioxidants or processes fats.", "The lab reports which variants you carry, and a formula is compounded from nutrients chosen for those results. Your ND checks the formula against your medications and existing supplements, then reviews it with you over time. Research on this approach is still developing."], "w": ["Personalised supplement planning", "Methylation and B-vitamin needs (MTHFR)", "Replacing several separate supplements with one formula", "Prevention planning"]},
"selfdecode": {"a": ["SelfDecode is a precision-health platform that pairs an at-home DNA test with an AI health GPT. The GPT is a chat-style artificial-intelligence assistant that analyses your genetic data together with your lab results, lifestyle and goals.", "At Mediworks, your Naturopathic Doctor uses SelfDecode as an analysis tool. Every recommendation is reviewed by your ND and fitted to your history, symptoms and medications."], "h": ["Whole genome sequencing reads your entire genome rather than selected markers. Hereditary disease findings, such as BRCA1/2, are screening results that are confirmed with clinical testing. Reports also cover areas such as methylation, nutrient needs, sleep, exercise response and inherited tendencies.", "Your ND can add your bloodwork and health information, then ask the GPT questions about your data, such as which nutrients matter most for your methylation genes. Its answers are a starting point for your ND's judgement, not a diagnosis."], "w": ["Understanding genetic tendencies", "Methylation and nutrient needs (such as MTHFR)", "Connecting DNA with your bloodwork", "Personalised diet, sleep and exercise planning", "Prevention planning"]}};
